\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Chile intervention \highlight\uc2  gives room for adjustments-cbank\b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Januar 2011\par 13:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Cbank chief reiterates \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  exceptional\par \par \uc2  * Cenbank says past cap controls effect "limited at best"  (Recast; Adds details on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  move)\par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO, Jan 17 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jose De Gregorio said on Monday a $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should give room for adjustments of the real economy as external risks remain high.\par \par \uc2  The bank started to purchase dollars on Jan. 5 to tame the strong peso, which is hurting exporters in the major fruit, wine and salmon producing nation.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to have a temporary effect on the peso, which weakened over 6 percent in the week that the bank announced it was going to start buying dollars.\par \par \uc2  De Gregorio said the effects of capital controls in the 1990s proved to be "limited at best," hinting that the bank may not immediately use other tools to further weaken the peso.\par \par \uc2  The bank's surprise move to hold its benchmark rate at 3.25 percent last week was seem by the market as an effort to complement the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  The peso was off 0.2 percent on Monday, trading at 490.00/490.50 per dollar after erasing steep losses on Friday following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate pause.  (Reporting by Simon Gardner and Brad Haynes; Writing by Alonso Soto; Editing by 