\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Chile  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Holds Key Rate At 3.25%\b0\par\par\uc2 496 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 2011\par 22:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 13 Jan 2011 16:02 EDT *DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 : Peso Has Depreciated On \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 13 Jan 2011 16:03 EDT *DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 : Rate Increases To Continue In Coming Months\par \par \uc2 13 Jan 2011 16:05 EDT *DJ  Chile \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 : Future Rate Hikes Depend On Domestic, External Macroeconomics\par \par \uc2 13 Jan 2011 16:05 EDT *DJ  Chile \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 : Private Expectations See Inflation Rising\par \par \uc2 13 Jan 2011 16:07 EDT *DJ  Chile \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 : Core Inflation Remains Limited\par \par \uc2 13 Jan 2011 16:28 EDT =DJ  Chile \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Holds Key Rate At 3.25%\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TPM Rate History (annual percentage): \par Jan    Dec    Nov   Oct    Sep   Aug   July  June  May \par 3.25%  3.25%  3.0%  2.75%  2.5%  2.0%  1.5%  1.0%  0.5% \par  \par  \par   By Anthony Esposito \par   Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Following a recently announced $12 billion \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  program for 2011, the Chilean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held its benchmark interest rate steady on Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At its monthly monetary policy meeting Thursday, the bank kept the benchmark overnight rate, known locally as the TPM, at 3.25%, the bank's first pause since it started withdrawing its monetary stimulus in June last year following the massive stimulus that began in 2009.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Only half of the 10 analysts polled earlier in the week by Dow Jones Newswires saw the bank pausing its rate increases, while the other half expected the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to raise the TPM 25 basis points to 3.5%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 monetary authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pointed out that its program to increase its foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves by $12 billion this year has weakened the peso versus the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the first days following the announcement of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Jan. 3, the peso lost over 7% against the dollar, although it has regained some territory in recent sessions as international copper prices rise.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said that private expectations for inflation have risen, particularly in the short term.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Earlier this week, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  released its monthly analysts' survey of economic expectations and its bi-weekly traders' survey. Both surveys showed private-sector inflation expectations have increased, with analysts seeing 3.6% inflation by the end of the year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The outlook is higher than the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's 3.3% year-end inflation expectations.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Core inflation remains limited, though, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's post-meeting communique said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The core consumer price index gained 0.3% in December from the previous month. For the year, core CPI, which factors out volatile fresh produce and fuel prices, rose 2.5% on the year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reiterated that it will be necessary to continue removing the monetary stimulus in coming months, although the "rhythm will depend on domestic and external macroeconomic conditions."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 13, 2011 16:28 ET (21:28 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110113e71d005b3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
