\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Chile's peso up on rate move, Mexican peso dips\b0\par\par\uc2 568 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 2011\par 14:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real and Chilean peso both gain 0.5 pct\par \par \uc2 * Mexican peso dips 0.2 pct after U.S. jobs data\par \par \uc2 (Adds comments, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Maria Jose Latorre\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/SANTIAGO, Jan 13 (Reuters) - Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed on Thursday, helped by bets the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would hike interest rates, drawing in yield-hungry investors even as policymakers \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also supported by successful bond auctions in Spain and Italy that helped to ease euro zone fiscal concerns, while Mexico's peso dipped on a rise in U.S. jobless claims.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=> firmed 0.47 percent to 488.20 per dollar as some investors in a divided market bet that Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hike its benchmark interest rate for the eighth consecutive time later on Thursday. [ID:nN13261867c]\par \par \uc2 "There should be an increase of 25 points," said Rodrigo Sarria, a trader at Celfin Capital in Santiago. "And we should keep seeing increases from here onward, especially because of the inflation pressures," he added.\par \par \uc2 Others think policymakers will leave borrowing costs steady so as not to lure even more hot money to the country and undermine the $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan launched last week that knocked the peso off a nearly three year high.\par \par \uc2 Broadly supporting bids for riskier assets, Spain sold 3 billion euros of five-year bonds, raising the maximum amount targeted. Italy's auction of 5- and 15-year government bonds also went well. [ID:nLDE70C0IA].\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> was bid 0.48 percent stronger at 1.667 reais per U.S. dollar on the local spot market.\par \par \uc2 "The worries over Europe are diminishing a little... I'm not seeing any real difference to yesterday, we're continuing on the same track," said Alfredo Barbutti, an economist at the BGC Liquidez brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 However, investors were reluctant to push the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  much higher in case it triggered more aggressive government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, he said.\par \par \uc2 MEXICAN PESO RETREATS FROM 2-YR HIGH\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <MXN=> slipped 0.21 percent to 12.0965 per dollar after jobless claims in the United States, Mexico's main trading partner, jumped to their highest level since October. [ID:nN13271305]\par \par \uc2 The news helped weaken the peso after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit its strongest level since Oct. 2008 in the previous session. But overall, U.S. data was mixed, with higher producer prices and a jump in U.S. exports.\par \par \uc2 "The fact that there was inflation in the United States tells you the economy is recovering and it is not all bad," said Antonio Magana, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at brokerage Interacciones.\par \par \uc2 The peso has won favor among investors since it is one of the few \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region which is not at risk from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, Mexico's free-market orthodoxy has not been challenged too much with the peso barely clawing back from pre-crisis levels.\par \par \uc2 If the peso reaches 11.50 per dollar, the Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could take measures similar to Chile's dollar-buying plan, said Benito Berber, an economist at Nomura in New York.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Michael O'Boyle in Mexico City)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110116e71d0009j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
