\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:OppenheimerFunds Cuts Brazil, Mexico Sovereign-Debt Exposure\b0\par\par\uc2 723 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2011\par 19:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Updates with firm's complete name in first paragraph.)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Anjali Cordeiro \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--OppenheimerFunds's emerging-market bond funds have sold all their Mexican and Brazilian sovereign-debt holdings, and are paring exposure to \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of countries \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, a senior portfolio manager for the firm said in an interview.\par \par \uc2 Sara Zervos--who oversees about $11 billion in emerging-market debt for OppenheimerFunds and is among the biggest emerging-market portfolio managers in the U.S.--said her funds have reduced their exposure to Chile's peso and Brazil's real as central bankers in these countries take steps to prevent their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from appreciating.\par \par \uc2 The funds she manages cut their exposure to Brazil and Mexico sovereign bonds at the end of last year because they see little room for substantial returns on these assets, whose spreads with Treasurys are already narrow. In search of higher returns in emerging markets, her emerging-market teams are moving more money to higher yielding emerging-market corporate debt. For exposure to Brazil and Mexico, her funds now own only corporate debt from those countries.\par \par \uc2 Zervos's funds can also invest in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds to get exposure to a country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and benefit from any potential appreciation. Her funds are increasing their exposure to the South African rand, partly because it stands to benefit from increased demand for commodities.\par \par \uc2 Zervos's comments highlight the changing landscape that emerging-market fund managers are facing as money rushes into these fast-growing regions. As more money has moved to the developing world, spreads between emerging-market sovereign bonds and Treasurys have tightened significantly, making it harder to project big returns on such investments. Meanwhile, the surge in capital flows to developing countries has driven up their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pushing local policymakers in countries from Brazil to \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. That is making emerging-market investing more challenging.\par \par \uc2 "Last year was a pure rebound year, extending from 2009. We got through the double-dip fear and then it was all ships ahead," she said. "But this year we are worried about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we are worried about central banks being behind the curve and it makes the outlook much trickier."\par \par \uc2 Earlier in January, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced that it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with plans to increase its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves by $12 billion in 2011 in an effort to hold down the peso and assuage the worries of Chile's exporters.\par \par \uc2 Zervos, who is based in New York, said her funds had a small exposure to \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso, which she completely erased right after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was announced, even though she has a strong fundamental outlook for the Chilean peso. Along similar lines she has cut back exposure her funds have to the Brazilian real via local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, bringing down that allocation to marketweight from overweight.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently moved to reduce the size of banks' bets in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to protect the financial system and investors have grown more concerned that the government will be more aggressive in halting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gain.\par \par \uc2 "There might be every macro reason in the world to love the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the randomness of policy to try and stop appreciation makes us want to have a smaller position," Zervos said.\par \par \uc2 Zervos, an emerging-markets veteran, is portfolio manager of the Oppenheimer International Bond Fund, Oppenheimer Emerging Markets Debt Fund, and Oppenheimer Global Strategic Income Fund. Her comments underscore how countries risk pushing even longer term investors away when they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 "I tend to be more overweight stories with good fundamentals plus lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," she said. She is bullish on the Mexican peso on expectations that the U.S. economy will keep recovering and pull Mexico with it. Also, Mexican authorities don't interfere with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Zervos says despite her more cautious tone on Brazilian sovereign bonds, she is bullish on corporate debt from the country. "That's where the best bang for the buck is," she said, referring to high yield emerging-market corporate bonds.\par \par \uc2 -By Anjali Cordeiro, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2200; anjali.cordeiro@dowjones.com [ 12-01-11 1852GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110112e71c001di\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
