\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Chile To See Rate Hike, Stronger Peso -Bulltick\b0\par\par\uc2 158 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2011\par 20:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 1912 GMT [Dow Jones] Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely hike its benchmark interest rate on Thursday by 25 basis points to 3.5%, since Chile's peso has been responsive to the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts and economic growth remains robust, Bulltick Research said in a note. Still, the peso's decline may be short-lived, especially in light of pressure Tuesday from strong copper prices. "If commodity prices continue to rise this year (5%-10% in our expectation) and Chile posts strong economic growth of 6.0% as we expect, appreciation pressures will continue," pushing USD/CLP to 465," Bulltick said. But \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not follow in Brazil's footsteps with further \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures like capital restrictions, the note added.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com) \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Robert Flint, 212-416-2216; \par robert.flint@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 [ 11-01-11 1912GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1085   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110111e71b001eh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
