ening expected this year. (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2020 GMT [Dow Jones] S&P could upgrade Colombia's foreign long-term debt rating from BB+ to BBB- in the future, said S&P sovereign ratings head Joydeep Mukherji in a conference call. "We're signaling that Colombia potentially could be the next sovereign in Latin America to join the investment grade category," he said. Crucial factors in boosting the rating include GDP growth rates that demonstrate a solid economy, controlled government spending, and a fiscal situation that reflects a booming energy sector, the analyst said. "Crossing from BB+ to BBB- is a sticky passage," he added, so S&P will examine Colombia's ability to withstand stress tests over the next three to five years. (erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2016 GMT [Dow Jones] Most traders are focused on getting over the hump of Wednesday's Portuguese debt auction, but Spain and Italy are also due to sell securities this week. Analysts at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Western Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  say this makes for a mix that will see the euro "spike" in volatility. "Amid the uncertainty, many traders with large short positions will trim their exposures, while others will seek to place new bets on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's direction--leading to choppy trading conditions. Sharp reversals are common in this sort of environment, making it a good time to consider placing limit orders," the firm said in a research note.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (javier.david@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2013 GMT [Dow Jones] Sovereign credit default swaps on Slovenia are 6.58BP wider, or 7.6% worse, Tuesday, according to CMA DataVision. The country sold EUR1.5 billion in new 10-year bonds Monday, at 125 bps over midswaps, according to a person familiar with the deal. The deal was reportedly oversubscribed, but jitters about the amount of supply coming from other European nations issuing debt may have unnerved investors.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (katy.burne@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1955 GMT [Dow Jones] The front end of the government of Canada curve is vulnerable to a sell-off on growing evidence of acceleration of Canadian economic growth, says Bank of America/Merrill Lynch. "As a result, we continue to favor calendar steepeners and outright short positions in the 2-year note, with a target of 100bp for the 2-year/ overnight curve (vs spot 77bp)," it says. "The long end of the curve continues to be dominated by foreign investor purchases," Merrill adds. (don.curren@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0024 GMT [Dow Jones] NZD/USD to track any moves in AUD, with Australian climatic conditions dominating \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  direction, says ANZ Senior Dealer Alex Sinton. ANZ economists estimate the floods would shave at least 0.5% off 1Q GDP, with a net loss of 0.3% of GDP over 2011. Pair last at 0.7592 vs 0.7587 late Tuesday. Says any topside levels above 0.7650 remain out of reach until such time as markets fully price the impact of the Queensland flooding. Sinton tips a range of 0.7565-0.7635 short term. (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1916 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2  unit Banamex has raised its economic growth estimate for Mexico in 2011 to 4.8% from 3.9%, citing expectations of higher growth in the U.S. As a result, Banamex expects consumer price inflation of 3.9%, up from it previous estimate of 3.5%, and expects that the Bank of Mexico will start raising its overnight rate from the current 4.5% in October, instead of waiting until 2012. Banamex sees the overnight rate reaching 5% by year-end. (Anthony.harrup@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1912 GMT [Dow Jones] Chile's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will likely hike its benchmark interest rate on Thursday by 25 basis points to 3.5%, since Chile's peso has been responsive to the government's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  efforts and economic growth remains robust, Bulltick Research said in a note. Still, the peso's decline may be short-lived, especially in light of pressure Tuesday from strong copper prices. "If commodity prices continue to rise this year (5%-10% in our expectation) and Chile posts strong economic growth of 6.0% as we expect, appreciation pressures will continue," pushing USD/CLP to 465," Bulltick said. But \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will not follow in Brazil's footsteps with further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventionist\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  measures like capital restrictions, the note added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1859 GMT [Dow Jones] Interest rates in Sri Lanka will eventually move up in 2011, even though the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unexpectedly cut its two policy rates Tuesday, say analysts with Capital Economics. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  anticipates that food price pressures will ease in coming months while high investment will reduce capacity constraints, but "We are not so sure," Capital Economics notes. Their best guess is that rates will rise from mid-year. (anjali.cordeiro@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1856 GMT [Dow Jones] After jumping within view of overnight highs near $1.30, the euro resumed its slide to change hands around $1.2950. Dealers say the $1.30 figure is providing stiff near-term resistance amid the market's nervousness about Portuguese debt auction on Wednesday. However, the single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is holding onto sharp gains against Japanese yen around 107.90.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (javier.david@dowjones.com) [ 01-11-11 1524ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110111e71b000da\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
