\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: AUD Moves To Dictate Direction Of NZD/USD On Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,122 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2011\par 20:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0024 GMT [Dow Jones] NZD/USD to track any moves in AUD, with Australian climatic conditions dominating \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  direction, says ANZ Senior Dealer Alex Sinton. ANZ economists estimate the floods would shave at least 0.5% off 1Q GDP, with a net loss of 0.3% of GDP over 2011. Pair last at 0.7592 vs 0.7587 late Tuesday. Says any topside levels above 0.7650 remain out of reach until such time as markets fully price the impact of the Queensland flooding. Sinton tips a range of 0.7565-0.7635 short term. (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1916 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  unit Banamex has raised its economic growth estimate for Mexico in 2011 to 4.8% from 3.9%, citing expectations of higher growth in the U.S. As a result, Banamex expects consumer price inflation of 3.9%, up from it previous estimate of 3.5%, and expects that the Bank of Mexico will start raising its overnight rate from the current 4.5% in October, instead of waiting until 2012. Banamex sees the overnight rate reaching 5% by year-end. (Anthony.harrup@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1912 GMT [Dow Jones] Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely hike its benchmark interest rate on Thursday by 25 basis points to 3.5%, since Chile's peso has been responsive to the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts and economic growth remains robust, Bulltick Research said in a note. Still, the peso's decline may be short-lived, especially in light of pressure Tuesday from strong copper prices. "If commodity prices continue to rise this year (5%-10% in our expectation) and Chile posts strong economic growth of 6.0% as we expect, appreciation pressures will continue," pushing USD/CLP to 465," Bulltick said. But \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not follow in Brazil's footsteps with further \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures like capital restrictions, the note added.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1859 GMT [Dow Jones] Interest rates in Sri Lanka will eventually move up in 2011, even though the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unexpectedly cut its two policy rates Tuesday, say analysts with Capital Economics. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  anticipates that food price pressures will ease in coming months while high investment will reduce capacity constraints, but "We are not so sure," Capital Economics notes. Their best guess is that rates will rise from mid-year. (anjali.cordeiro@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1856 GMT [Dow Jones] After jumping within view of overnight highs near $1.30, the euro resumed its slide to change hands around $1.2950. Dealers say the $1.30 figure is providing stiff near-term resistance amid the market's nervousness about Portuguese debt auction on Wednesday. However, the single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is holding onto sharp gains against Japanese yen around 107.90.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (javier.david@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1833 GMT [Dow Jones] Some buyers are now coming back to the Treasury market, hearted by the decent 3-year auction. Bond prices move further away from session lows but still down for the session as more supply weighs. In recent trade, the benchmark 10-year note is 12/32 lower to yield 3.336%. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1827 GMT [Dow Jones] Credit default swaps on Portugal tightened to 537 bps from their record wide close of 555 bps Monday, but mainly because the ECB was in the market buying up Portuguese debt, according to Gavan Nolan, in credit analysis at data provider Markit. All eyes are on Wednesday's EUR1.25 bln debt auction from the nation, he added, and it's unclear how the CDS will perform. Portugal is "likely the next bailout candidate," according to strategists at Janney Capital Markets. The 10-year bonds are expected to price around 7%, which is "a level that's viewed as unsustainable," according to Anthony Valeri, fixed-income strategist at LPL Financial. (katy.burne@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1824 GMT [Dow Jones] US interest rate futures prices mostly lower and little changed even as market adquately absorbs $32 bln in 3-yr Tsy notes. Concessions remain in play as traders await $21 bln 10-yr Tsy note auction Wed and $13 bln 30-yr Tsy bond auction Thurs. Mar classic Tsy bond futures, covering 15 to 25-yr maturities, hover a little above morning low of 120-09. Mar 10-yr Tsy notes stay close to morning low of 120-12+. Quarterly 2012 through 2014 Eurodollar futures recently down 1.5 to 4 BP. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1823 GMT [Dow Jones] The bond market shrugs off a decent 3-year sale as more supply is coming up. There is $21-bln 10-yr sale due Wednesday and a $13-bln 30-yr bond Thursday. Demand for long maturity sales have been volatile. In recent trade, the benchmark 10-year note is 17/32 lower to yield 3.355%. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1804 GMT [Dow Jones] We don't know if one can really read anything into these numbers, but it may be worth noting that California GOs have improved over the last year while Illinois debt has worsened considerably. These are the two lowest rated states. According Janney Capital Markets data, California spreads to a generic 10-year triple-A muni fell 21 bps between Jan. 4, 2010 and Jan. 4, 2011, while Illinois' spread rose 115 bps. The higher an issue goes in yield, the lower the price, so the market seems to be reflecting a different opinion of California than of Illinois. California credit default swaps in the same period fell by 51 bps, while Illinois CDS soared 191 bps, according to Markit. CDS levels represent the cost in bps to protect against bankruptcy, so rising costs indicate greater fear, although the muni CDS market is a relatively quiet space. (stan.rosenberg@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1804 GMT [Dow Jones] Treasurys hold losses trading near session lows after 3-year sale. Demand for the auction is decent. In recent trade, the benchmark 10-year note is 19/32 lower to yield 3.363%. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1803 GMT [Dow Jones] The indirect bid - a proxy for demand from foreign buyers including central banks - for the three-year note was 39%, compared to the average of 35.8% for the past four auctions. The direct bid, a category of bids from non-primary dealers, banks, money managers and depository institutions who have direct accounts to submit bids to the Treasury auctions, was 16%, compared to the average of 13.9% for the past four auctions. (min.zeng@dowjones.com) [ 01-11-11 1424ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110111e71b000cp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
