\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  c.bank chief: no plan to up peso  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 205 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2011\par 16:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BASEL, Jan 10 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has no plans to increase the size of its $12 billion programme aimed at curbing the rise of the peso but the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not solve the problem of underlying appreciation pressure, its governor said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Jose de Gregorio said recent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  had had the intended impact but added that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tensions were likely to remain as the country's economy improves at a faster rate than those in more developed regions.\par \par \uc2 "The programme has two components: one is the objective of reserve accumulation and we have stated that 12 billion is an appropriate figure. That's what we are planning to do as \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and no further plans of changing that amount," he told reporters on the sidelines of a meeting of central bankers.\par \par \uc2 "We have been very clear that this has no permanent effect. As long as the world remains in the state as it is now we need some domestic adjustment because the tensions will persist." (Reporting by Marc Jones and Sven Egenter; editing by Patrick Graham)\par \par \uc2 CHILE/ (URGENT)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|U|NAT|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110110e71a0011p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
