\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging-Mkt Debt Move Little Against Tsys;  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed\b0\par\par\uc2 By Erin McCarthy   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 657 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2011\par 21:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Emerging-market debt saw little change on Monday against Treasurys, which continued to rise on the euro zone's sovereign-debt concerns, while key Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw mixed results after initial losses.\par \par \uc2 On Monday afternoon, the risk premium, or spread, on the \uc2 J.P. Morgan\uc2  Emerging Markets Bond Index Global, or Embig, widened just three basis points to 285 basis points over U.S. Treasurys. In price terms, the index slipped 0.16% on the day.\par \par \uc2 Worries that Portugal's debt woes could spread to larger economies in the euro zone drove investors toward U.S. Treasurys and made them more cautious about riskier assets in emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 Investors are still holding long positions on emerging-market debt, said Paul Biszko, analyst with \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "There's some hesitation or caution to add to those positions in recent weeks ... given the uncertainties on the euro-zone front," he added.\par \par \uc2 Mexico was in focus as its National Statistics Institute, or Inegi, reported Monday that its global economic activity indicator rose 4.3% on the year in October. The increase, however, marked a slowdown from the previous months as the rebound in industrial production lost steam, while growth in services picked up.\par \par \uc2 Analysts still expect Mexico to have a good growth year in 2011, nonetheless.\par \par \uc2 "Only major accidents around the world will keep Mexico's economy growing below trend," said Bulltick Research in a note.\par \par \uc2 On the Embig, Mexico's spread barely changed, tightening just one basis point to 154 basis points over Treasurys. In price terms, its index was flat.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso, meanwhile, pared back earlier losses, as it stood nearly flat at MXN12.2145 against the dollar Monday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's debt also saw little change on the Embig; its spread widened a modest two basis points over Treasurys. Its index was flat.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real, however, weakened significantly on expectations of further \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The real slid 0.32% to BRL1.6878 Monday afternoon, from BRL1.6825 the previous day.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the Brazilian government authorized the use of the sovereign fund to take on a role in both the spot market and the futures market for the real, raising speculation the government may start using reverse swap auctions to try to stem the appreciation of the real.\par \par \uc2 A reverse swap auction is a form of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market. At the auction, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps futures contracts linked to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions to contracts indexed to interest rates.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  report cited \uc2 Moody's\uc2  analyst Mauro Leos on Monday as saying Brazil's rating could be considered for an upgrade in April, "as long as the government curbs spending to meet its fiscal target and acts against inflation."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts also continue, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchasing $50 million on the local market Monday as part of its program to increase its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves by $12 billion this year.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso ended at CLP498.60 to the dollar, compared with Friday's close of CLP497.60. It was the first session the peso weakened in intraday trading to the CLP500 level since early September.\par \par \uc2 On the Embig, Chile's spread widened by seven basis points to 121 basis points over Treasurys. Its index dropped 0.33%.\par \par \uc2 Venezuela's spread also changed by slightly wider margins, by seven basis points to 1142 basis points over Treasurys. Its index declined 0.15%.\par \par \uc2 Venezuela ended 2010 with an inflation rate of 27.2%, higher than the 25.1% rate of 2009, according to statistics the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Venezuela\uc2  released last week.\par \par \uc2 -By Erin McCarthy, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2712; erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (Anthony Harrup, Matthew Cowley, Cynthia Lin and Anthony Esposito contributed to this article.) [ 10-01-11 2045GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1810 4071   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110110e71a001kg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
