\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Chile peso slumps 6 pct in week, Mexico peso up\b0\par\par\uc2 561 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2011\par 14:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  hammers peso to 4-month low\par \par \uc2 * Brazil real slides 1.2 percent in week\par \par \uc2 * Mexican peso gains 1 percent on U.S. outlook (Adds comments, updates prices, changes dateline, previous SAO PAULO/MEXICO CITY)\par \par \uc2 By Brad Haynes and Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO/MEXICO CITY, Jan 7 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Chile and Brazil posted steep losses this week after officials stepped up efforts to sap those units' strength, while Mexico's peso rose on the improving outlook for the U.S. economy.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso ended Friday at a 4-month low after policymakers threw their muscle into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with daily dollar purchases, knocking the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down 6 percent in its worst weekly slide in almost 2 years. For details see [ID:nN30113748].\par \par \uc2 The market is divided about whether Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could hike interest rates next week to cool rising inflation or if it could leave borrowing costs steady so as not to boost the attraction of its debt to yield hungry investors.\par \par \uc2 "We think they will pause because they want to give credibility to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Roberto Melzi, an analyst at \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 Others are betting higher inflation, pushed up by rising food prices, could push the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hike. [ID:nN07198777]\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=> shed 0.44 percent to 497.50 per U.S. dollar on Friday.\par \par \uc2 After surging to a nearly three-year high before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move this week, analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be range-bound between 470 and 510 or so as attraction to \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strong economy is tempered by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks.\par \par \uc2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Graphic on region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/cat64r"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/cat64r}}}\uc2  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> bid 0.12 percent weaker to 1.684 per dollar, capping a 1.2 percent loss for the week after the latest measure to stem the real's strength by authorities, who have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2009.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday it will impose an unremunerated reserve requirement of 60 percent on U.S. dollar short positions when certain limits are exceeded. [ID:nN0697246]\par \par \uc2 "Regardless of whether the latest measures prove effective or not, one thing is clear: regulatory uncertainty is rising, and investors are asking, 'What next'? " wrote analysts at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  in a research note.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <MXN=> was little changed on Friday, dipping 0.02 percent to 12.2324 per dollar and on track to post a gain of around 1 percent for the week.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso firmed this week on signs the U.S. economy may grow more than expected this year, and it has also been supported by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Brazil as they boost the attraction to Mexico's free-floating market.\par \par \uc2 "You can make a pretty bullish case for Mexico," said Win Thin, an emerging markets strategist at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 The peso touched an 8-month high on Thursday and it may be poised to soon hit its highest levels in more than two years, Thin said. (Additional reporting by Jean Luis Arce in Mexico City and Samantha Pearson in Sao Paulo; Editing by James Dalgleish)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|U|ABX|BNX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110110e717000td\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
