\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil real hit by  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  rule, Chile stabilizes\b0\par\par\uc2 589 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 2011\par 14:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Brazil's cenbank imposes new rule on banks' \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions\par \par \uc2 * Real drops 0.78 pct, Mexican peso loses 0.4 pct\par \par \uc2 * Chile's peso stabilizes after huge losses (Updates prices, adds comments)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Nathalia Ferreira\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Jan 6 (Reuters) - Brazil's real sank on Thursday after officials said they would make it more expensive for banks to continue to bet on the fast-rising \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso stabilized after this week's government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  imposed a reserve requirement on banks' short positions on the U.S. dollar, turning up the heat on speculators authorities blame for overvaluing the real. For details, see [ID:nLDE7050Z6] and [ID:nN06102054].\par \par \uc2 "It is not the most powerful measure, but it is one more, and the threat is there that they could do even more," said Roberto Melzi, a strategist at Barclay's Capital in New York.\par \par \uc2 The country has been buying dollars in daily auctions and also raised taxes on foreign investments.\par \par \uc2 Like many emerging Latin and Asian economies, Brazil has struggled with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation that has made its exports more difficult to sell abroad and flooded the country with cheap imports.\par \par \uc2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 Graphic on region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/cat64r"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/cat64r}}}\par \par \uc2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 Banks have 90 days to get ready for the new rules, meaning there was not a mad rush to reduce positions.\par \par \uc2 "It won't necessarily change the trend -- it could hold the market back a little," said Jose Carlos Amado, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at the Renascenca brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 The real <BRBY> was bid 0.78 percent weaker at 1.686 per dollar, extending losses as investors broadly bet in favor of the greenback ahead of Friday's U.S. monthly payrolls data for December.\par \par \uc2 The jobs report could support the view that the U.S. economy is growing faster than expected.\par \par \uc2 Expectations of better U.S. growth have pushed up U.S. bond yields, making dollar investments more attractive compared to higher-yielding, but riskier, emerging market assets.\par \par \uc2 CHILE'S PESO STABILIZES\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=> stabilized after two days of sharp drops, shedding 0.04 percent to 495.20, its weakest close in more than three months. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost 6 percent of its value against the dollar and suffered its worst one-day plunge in a quarter century since \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  unveiled its plan to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Tuesday. [ID:nN30113748]\par \par \uc2 "The market has calmed, and we're not seeing the exuberance of the first days," said one trader in Santiago.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts expect the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be range-bound between around 510 and 470 per dollar for now as investors are drawn to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strong economy but also worry about further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso <MXN=> hit an eight-month high early in the session but then fell as the dollar broadly gained. The peso weakened 0.4 percent to 12.2340 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Analysts at some banks see the Mexican peso soon firming to a more than two-year high and then breaking past the 12-per dollar per level.\par \par \uc2 Even with such gains, the peso remains below the levels it traded at before the 2008 financial crisis, easing concerns that officials could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  any time soon. (Additional reporting by Michael O'Boyle in Mexico City and Frolin Romero and Brad Haynes in Santiago; Editing by Padraic Cassidy)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|ABN|D|M   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110109e7160007c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
