\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  peso takes breather after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  plunge\b0\par\par\uc2 661 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 2011\par 13:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Peso trades shade stronger after dropping 6 pct\par \par \uc2 * Cenbank conducts 2nd auction in $12 bln \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Updates with peso close, monetary policy implications)\par \par \uc2 By Froilan Romero and Brad Haynes\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Jan 6 (Reuters) - The Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed broadly flat on Thursday, taking a breather after falling about 6 percent in two days following a $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 The world's No. 1 copper producer followed Brazil, Peru and Colombia in drafting measures to rein in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as so-called hot money poured into the fast-growing emerging market countries. The Chilean peso <CLP=CL> soared 17 percent against the dollar in the second half of 2010.\par \par \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted its second $50 million auction to buy dollars on Thursday, paying an average of 493.84 pesos per dollar. The first phase of the auctions will last until Feb. 9.\par \par \uc2 "The market has calmed and we're not seeing the exuberance of the first days," said one trader. "I think after that first wave, where the market was moving on capital flows, now it will be looking to foreign markets."\par \par \uc2 The peso gained as much as 0.5 percent before settling to close flat on Thursday, bidding 495.3 per dollar. The bank announced its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a near three-year high of 465.5 per dollar on Monday. ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 > For a TAKE-A-LOOK, see [ID:nN30113748]\par \par \uc2 > For a graphic, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/cat64r"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/cat64r}}}\uc2  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Brazilian real <BRBY> weakened sharply on Thursday after its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made its boldest move so far to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains, imposing reserve requirements on banks' short positions on U.S. dollars. For details, see [ID:nLDE7050Z6]\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso sank 4.5 percent on Tuesday, its biggest daily drop in more than 25 years, in the first day of trading after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced plans to buy $12 billion in greenbacks in installments to help exporters. [ID:nN04206531]\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 's effect would be transitory as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the world's commodity exporters continue to appreciate.\par \par \uc2 Analysts see the exchange rate slipping as far as 510 pesos per dollar in the coming months before reverting to an equilibrium closer to 470 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Long-term local debt yields rose after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced it would sterilize, or offset, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by issuing new debt. The market's implicit inflation expectations also jumped as investors bet that the rising effective cost of imports would hit consumer prices.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cited the peso's appreciation as a factor containing inflation last year amid a robust recovery, allowing the bank to slow the pace of its interest rate hikes.\par \par \uc2 But Finance Minister Felipe Larrain said on Wednesday he didn't expect the weaker exchange rate to boost inflation.\par \par \uc2 "The firming exchange rate wasn't entirely reflected in prices, so the weakening of the exchange rate after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcement won't be reflected in prices either," said Larrain.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Jose de Gregorio also said this week that the bank would continue managing monetary policy to target inflation "without restrictions."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's last market poll showed traders closely divided on whether the bank will opt for a pause or an eighth consecutive rate raise at its Jan. 13 rate-setting meeting.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is more likely to hold its benchmark rate in order to bolster the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Others see the dollar purchase program adequately addressing the peso's strength, giving the bank room to continue raising rates after the economy grew faster than expected in November.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  weighed holding the rate in December, according to bank minutes, though market rate futures point to another 25 basis point increase to 3.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 CHILE-ECONOMY/PESO (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110106e7160013p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
