 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has made the country's export products too expensive in world markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (michael.crittenden@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1853 GMT [Dow Jones] The dollar gained broadly against its rivals after encouraging US data painted a brightening picture of the economy. The dollar soared to a two-week high against the yen and a one-week high against the euro before paring some of its gains in afternoon trading. The data heightened expectations that Friday's US non-farm payrolls report could deliver a positive surprise, said Jane Foley, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rabobank\f28 \uc2 \f2  in London. The euro was at $1.3165 from $1.3308 late Tuesday, according to EBS via CQG, down more than 1%. The dollar gained about 1.45% to trade at Y83.22 from Y82.05.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (bradley.davis@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1821 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's $12 bln \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could have a meaningful effect on the exchange rate, but it all depends on the global backdrop, said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America\f28 \uc2 \f2 Merrill Lynch\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysts in a research note. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  adds depreciation risks for the Chilean peso, but BoA \f28 \uc2 \f2 Merrill Lynch\f28 \uc2 \f2  is holding onto its year-end forecast for USD/CLP at 490.00. In addition, bets are on that Chile's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will pause its benchmark rate at its January monetary policy meeting, and will resume tightening after a month or two, ending 2011 with policy rates near 4.5%, the note said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1802 GMT [Dow Jones] T