t@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1737 GMT [Dow Jones] Volatilities implied by USD/JPY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  options were higher in NY Wed from Tokyo after the dollar rose strongly against the yen. One-month at-the-money USD/JPY options implied volatilities were at 10.0%/10.70%, from 9.95%/10.65% in Tokyo and from 10.0%/10.93% Tue in NY. One-month EUR/USD implied vols were at 13.30%/13.55%, from 13.0%/13.25% in Tokyo and from 13.0%/13.69% Tue in NY. One-month EUR/JPY implied vols were at 12.10%/14.10% unchanged from 12.10%/14.10% in Tokyo and from 12.85%/13.50% in NY Tue. (bradley.davis@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1734 GMT [Dow Jones] A head and shoulder pattern is forming on the daily EUR/CAD chart, with a neckline at 1.2970, said Matt Perrier of BMO Capital Markets in Toronto. EUR is steeply lower vs CAD, at 1.3107 in midday trading, from 1.3285 late Tues, according to CQG. BMO sees initial support "on the approach to the mid-June 1.2450 lows over the next 4 weeks should the pattern begin to unfold with a break of that level opening up next leg down towards target," he said. He notes a stop loss at 1.3600, above the right shoulder and the 55 day moving average, which has contained rallies since early Nov. (karen.johnson@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1732 GMT [Dow Jones] The ICE dollar Index is straining for a breakout, says Stephen Cox, chief technician for Dow Jones Newswires. "The ICE Dollar Index has put in a strong intraday rally Wednesday, and I believe that a relatively slight extension of the move would turn the daily chart bullish," Cox writes in CHARTING MARKETS. The Index is now trading at 80.084 and the chance of a test of 80.558 may be imminent. Support for a higher move is the 79.027-78.883 range. But a move below support would be targeting 77.675.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (robert.flint@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1729 GMT [Dow Jones] A profusion of covered bond deals along with the first senior bank debt transactions of 2011 and a deal from Renault's (RNO.FR) \f28 \uc2 \f2 RCI Banque\f28 \uc2 \f2  mean that Wednesday has been "the busiest primary market session in Europe for months," says Suki Mann at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Still, a couple of DCM bankers reckon high supply might be misleading. "The market is incredibly busy, but the signs are not necessarily in as good shape as people are making out," says one. "A lot of the bank deals are coming at the wider end of recent ranges, and without big over-subscription levels." (mark.brown@dowjones.com) [ 01-05-11 1419ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110105e715000d2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
