.brown@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1715 GMT [Dow Jones] Mexican stocks turned positive as markets digest positive jobs and other data in the US, leading USD/MXN to test support at 12.20. IPC index recently up 0.1% to 38,575 points, with USD/MXN quoted in Mexico City at 12.2005, according to Infosel. A \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader said good news in the US "is better news in Mexico" because of strong trade ties, but that USD/MXN is unlikely to break through 12.19, and would trade in the 12.19-12.24 range. (laurence.iliff@dowjones.com) [ 01-05-11 1418ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110105e715000d1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
