\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Obama, China's Hu To Discuss  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Policy\b0\par\par\uc2 1,284 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2011\par 20:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Robert Flint, 212-416-2216; \par robert.flint@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1916 GMT [Dow Jones] President Obama will press Chinese President Hu Jintao on Beijing's policy on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when the two meet at the White House in two weeks, White House spokesman Robert Gibbs said. The US continues to believe that China must take steps to allow its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the yuan, to continue to appreciate, said Gibbs. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy is a long-standing bone of contention between the two countries. The US views the yuan as artifically undervalued, while China is reluctant to loosen its hold on the yuan for fear of costing millions of Chinese workers their jobs because a stronger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has made the country's export products too expensive in world markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 (michael.crittenden@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1853 GMT [Dow Jones] The dollar gained broadly against its rivals after encouraging US data painted a brightening picture of the economy. The dollar soared to a two-week high against the yen and a one-week high against the euro before paring some of its gains in afternoon trading. The data heightened expectations that Friday's US non-farm payrolls report could deliver a positive surprise, said Jane Foley, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  in London. The euro was at $1.3165 from $1.3308 late Tuesday, according to EBS via CQG, down more than 1%. The dollar gained about 1.45% to trade at Y83.22 from Y82.05.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (bradley.davis@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1821 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's $12 bln \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could have a meaningful effect on the exchange rate, but it all depends on the global backdrop, said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America\f28 \uc2 \f2 Merrill Lynch\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysts in a research note. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  adds depreciation risks for the Chilean peso, but BoA \f28 \uc2 \f2 Merrill Lynch\f28 \uc2 \f2  is holding onto its year-end forecast for USD/CLP at 490.00. In addition, bets are on that Chile's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will pause its benchmark rate at its January monetary policy meeting, and will resume tightening after a month or two, ending 2011 with policy rates near 4.5%, the note said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1802 GMT [Dow Jones] The first round of new Treasury coupon supply in 2011 will hit the market next week and Treasury is set to announce the sizes Thursday morning. Primary dealer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects $66 bln in total, unchanged from last month. It will include $32 bln in three-year notes, $21 bln in 10-year notes and $13 bln in 30-year bonds. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1801 GMT [Dow Jones] After seeing the 297,000 gain in jobs reported this morning by ADP, some economists have marked up their forecasts for the December payroll number to be reported Friday by the Bureau of Labor Statistics. The median forecast is now for a gain of 150,000 new jobs last month, up from 140,000 expected pre-ADP.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (kathleen.madigan@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1759 GMT [Dow Jones] Foreign investment surged into Brazil in 2010, but the overall amount of money flowing into the Brazilian economy fell slightly due to diminished foreign trade receipts. According to data from the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , net foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  flowing into Brazil fell to $24.35 bln last year after ending 2009 at $28.73 bln. Brazil continued to see the benefit of heavy investment, as foreigners sought out attractive returns on local stocks and fixed-income securities. In an attempt to slow the appreciation of the real, Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has maintained a consistent effort to soak up dollars from the local market with daily dollar purchase auctions. (gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (robert.flint@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1737 GMT [Dow Jones] Volatilities implied by USD/JPY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  options were higher in NY Wed from Tokyo after the dollar rose strongly against the yen. One-month at-the-money USD/JPY options implied volatilities were at 10.0%/10.70%, from 9.95%/10.65% in Tokyo and from 10.0%/10.93% Tue in NY. One-month EUR/USD implied vols were at 13.30%/13.55%, from 13.0%/13.25% in Tokyo and from 13.0%/13.69% Tue in NY. One-month EUR/JPY implied vols were at 12.10%/14.10% unchanged from 12.10%/14.10% in Tokyo and from 12.85%/13.50% in NY Tue. (bradley.davis@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1734 GMT [Dow Jones] A head and shoulder pattern is forming on the daily EUR/CAD chart, with a neckline at 1.2970, said Matt Perrier of BMO Capital Markets in Toronto. EUR is steeply lower vs CAD, at 1.3107 in midday trading, from 1.3285 late Tues, according to CQG. BMO sees initial support "on the approach to the mid-June 1.2450 lows over the next 4 weeks should the pattern begin to unfold with a break of that level openin