\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Dollar Gains Broadly After Encouraging US Data\b0\par\par\uc2 1,290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2011\par 19:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Robert Flint, 212-416-2216; \par robert.flint@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1853 GMT [Dow Jones] The dollar gained broadly against its rivals after encouraging US data painted a brightening picture of the economy. The dollar soared to a two-week high against the yen and a one-week high against the euro before paring some of its gains in afternoon trading. The data heightened expectations that Friday's US non-farm payrolls report could deliver a positive surprise, said Jane Foley, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rabobank\f28 \uc2 \f2  in London. The euro was at $1.3165 from $1.3308 late Tuesday, according to EBS via CQG, down more than 1%. The dollar gained about 1.45% to trade at Y83.22 from Y82.05.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (bradley.davis@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1821 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's $12 bln \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could have a meaningful effect on the exchange rate, but it all depends on the global backdrop, said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America\f28 \uc2 \f2 Merrill Lynch\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysts in a research note. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  adds depreciation risks for the Chilean peso, but BoA \f28 \uc2 \f2 Merrill Lynch\f28 \uc2 \f2  is holding onto its year-end forecast for USD/CLP at 490.00. In addition, bets are on that Chile's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will pause its benchmark rate at its January monetary policy meeting, and will resume tightening after a month or two, ending 2011 with policy rates near 4.5%, the note said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1802 GMT [Dow Jones] The first round of new Treasury coupon supply in 2011 will hit the market next week and Treasury is set to announce the sizes Thursday morning. Primary dealer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects $66 bln in total, unchanged from last month. It will include $32 bln in three-year notes, $21 bln in 10-year notes and $13 bln in 30-year bonds. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1801 GMT [Dow Jones] After seeing the 297,000 gain in jobs reported this morning by ADP, some economists have marked up their forecasts for the December payroll number to be reported Friday by the Bureau of Labor Statistics. The median forecast is now for a gain of 150,000 new jobs last month, up from 140,000 expected pre-ADP.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (kathleen.madigan@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1759 GMT [Dow Jones] Foreign investment surged into Brazil in 2010, but the overall amount of money flowing into the Brazilian economy fell slightly due to diminished foreign trade receipts. According to data from the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , net foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  flowing into Brazil fell to $24.35 bln last year after ending 2009 at $28.73 bln. Brazil continued to see the benefit of heavy investment, as foreigners sought out attractive returns on local stocks and fixed-income securities. In an attempt to slow the appreciation of the real, Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has maintained a consistent effort to soak up dollars from the local market with daily dollar purchase auctions. (gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (robert.flint@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1737 GMT [Dow Jones] Volatilities implied by USD/JPY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  options were higher in NY Wed from Tokyo after the dollar rose strongly against the yen. One-month at-the-money USD/JPY options implied volatilities were at 10.0%/10.70%, from 9.95%/10.65% in Tokyo and from 10.0%/10.93% Tue in NY. One-month EUR/USD implied vols were at 13.30%/13.55%, from 13.0%/13.25% in Tokyo and from 13.0%/13.69% Tue in NY. One-month EUR/JPY implied vols were at 12.10%/14.10% unchanged from 12.10%/14.10% in Tokyo and from 12.85%/13.50% in NY Tue. (bradley.davis@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1734 GMT [Dow Jones] A head and shoulder pattern is forming on the daily EUR/CAD chart, with a neckline at 1.2970, said Matt Perrier of BMO Capital Markets in Toronto. EUR is steeply lower vs CAD, at 1.3107 in midday trading, from 1.3285 late Tues, according to CQG. BMO sees initial support "on the approach to the mid-June 1.2450 lows over the next 4 weeks should the pattern begin to unfold with a break of that level opening up next leg down towards target," he said. He notes a stop loss at 1.3600, above the right shoulder and the 55 day moving average, which has contained rallies since early Nov. (karen.johnson@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1732 GMT [Dow Jones] The ICE dollar Index is straining for a breakout, says Stephen Cox, chief technician for Dow Jones Newswires. "The ICE Dollar Index has put in a strong intraday rally Wednesday, and I believe that a relatively slight extension of the move would turn the daily chart bullish," Cox writes in CHARTING MARKETS. The Index is now trading at 80.084 and the chance of a test of 80.558 may be imminent. Support for a higher move is the 79.027-78.883 range. But a move below support would be targeting 77.675.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (robert.flint@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1729 GMT [Dow Jones] A profusion of covered bond deals along with the first senior bank debt transactions of 2011 and a deal from Renault's (RNO.FR) \f28 \uc2 \f2 RCI Banque\f28 \uc2 \f2  mean that Wednesday has been "the busiest primary market session in Europe for months," says Suki Mann at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Still, a couple of DCM bankers reckon high supply might be misleading. "The market is incredibly busy, but the signs are not necessarily in as good shape as people are making out," says one. "A lot of the bank deals are coming at the wider end of recent ranges, and without big over-subscription levels." (mark.brown@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1715 GMT [Dow Jones] Mexican stocks turned positive as markets digest positive jobs and other data in the US, leading USD/MXN to test support at 12.20. IPC index recently up 0.1% to 38,575 points, with USD/MXN quoted in Mexico City at 12.2005, according to Infosel. A \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader said good news in the US "is better news in Mexico" because of strong trade ties, but that USD/MXN is unlikely to break through 12.19, and would trade in the 12.19-12.24 range. (laurence.iliff@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1708 GMT [Dow Jones] Value remains in emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as many have tracked or outpaced their respective GDP growth, said RBC analysts in a research note. Still, Asia's pace of appreciation has generally failed to reflect its economic expansion. The Indonesian rupiah as one exception; it has appreciated above a rate that appears consistent with its trend GDP growth, according to RBC. Meanwhile, in Latin America, the Brazilian real is overvalued. RBC's list of attractively valued \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  includes all of CEE; RUB and TRY; MXN; KRW, IDR and MYR.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1704 GMT [Dow Jones] Treasury yields jump on strong ADP and they may rise further in coming months should data continue to be strong. "The economy is showing signs of improving," say Ted Ake, head of Treasury and Agency trading at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale SA\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "Friday's payrolls report is the key data. Should it turn out to be strong, it is likely to raise questions about how much longer" the Fed will conduct its Treasury buying program to stimulate the economy. Stronger data in coming weeks will also raise questions about when the Fed is going to turn around to start raising interest rates, says Ake, adding that 10-yr yield could re-test 4%, a level not seen since April 2009.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (min.zeng@dowjones.com) [ 01-05-11 1353ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110105e715000ct\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
