\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE: \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Fin Min: $12B  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Is Biggest In Local History\b0\par\par\uc2 560 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2011\par 15:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to add comments from the Finance Minister)\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's announced $12 billion local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't pressure inflation upwards as most local prices weren't adjusted to the strength the peso was showing against the dollar, Finance Minister Felipe Larrain said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Late Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced it would begin \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local market through sterilized dollar purchases throughout the year for a total $12 billion.\par \par \uc2 For most of the final two quarters of 2010, the peso traded at 31-month highs against the dollar, prompting calls for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as exporters lost competitiveness abroad.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean economy is highly dependent on its exports of natural resources such as copper, fertilizers, molybdenum, wood pulp, fresh fruit and wines.\par \par \uc2 Larrain noted that this was the biggest local \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that "massive" \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as this one tended to be successful.\par \par \uc2 "We've seen that for an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to have a real effect on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it has to be massive and this one is the largest in Chilean history," Larrain told reporters.\par \par \uc2 He added that the government "supported and appreciated the move," noting that the ministry and the autonomous \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  closely coordinate their measures.\par \par \uc2 As Finance Minister, Larrain by law sits in on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy meetings but doesn't vote on the bank's decisions.\par \par \uc2 The official declined to estimate just how much the peso could gain on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar purchases, which are scheduled to begin Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 In the Monday session, the peso firmed to close at a 32-month high against the dollar. In early Tuesday trading, the peso slid 4% versus the dollar in reaction to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcement.\par \par \uc2 Larrain added that several key sectors of the domestic economy were losing competitiveness as a result of the strong peso.\par \par \uc2 "While copper exporters are protected by high copper prices, the agricultural sector needed support," he said.\par \par \uc2 He added the government would continue with its own measures aimed at contributing to keeping the peso at competitive levels against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 These measures include curbing fiscal spending, keeping dollar financing at a minimum, improving financial legislation, and streamlining and modernizing certain areas of government.\par \par \uc2 "We have to generate long-term tools to support the peso's competitiveness," he said.\par \par \uc2 Recently, the ministry announced it would issue most of its 2011 debt on the local market. The 2011 fiscal budget set a $7.8-billion cap on sovereign debt this year and the Finance Ministry last week announced it would issue $6 billion in sovereign debt domestically.\par \par \uc2 Local debt issues, denominated in pesos, cut down dollar inflows and ease some of the pressure rising interest rates and robust economic growth put on the peso.\par \par \uc2 "We left a $1.8-billion margin for other issues like we did in 2010," Larrain said.\par \par \uc2 Last year, for the first time in nearly a decade, Chile issued sovereign debt on international markets. Of the total $1.5 billion it issued abroad, $500 million was placed in peso-denominated debt to take some pressure off of the strong local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 -By Carolina Pica, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8919; carolina.pica@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 04, 2011 09:02 ET (14:02 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110104e714002op\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
