\par\par \b \uc2 BUY OR SELL-Which Chilean assets to hold after  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  action?\b0\par\par\uc2 637 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2011\par 21:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Inflation expectations on the rise after \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Investors buying inflation protection, stocks\par \par \uc2 * Peso, government bonds to sell off\par \par \uc2 By Walter Brandimarte\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Jan 4 (Reuters) - Chilean assets offering protection against inflation have become a favorite among investors after the government said on Monday it will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to curb the strength of the peso.\par \par \uc2 The outlook for stocks remains positive, especially for exporters which should benefit from a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the short term.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the peso is poised to weaken a little further but it could resume its appreciation trend later in the year if commodity prices remain on the rise.\par \par \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said late on Monday it would buy $12 billion this year to tame the peso, which has gained more than 17 percent against the U.S. dollar since the end of June.\par \par \uc2 Here is a compilation of the main trade ideas floated by analysts following the announcement:\par \par \uc2 BUY\par \par \uc2 * Protection against inflation\par \par \uc2 Inflation expectations are on the rise as a weaker peso will translate into higher prices of imported goods in the short term. In the longer run, investors are also likely to demand a higher inflation premium on government bonds if expectations of a pause in the cycle of monetary tightening are confirmed next week.\par \par \uc2 "If you interrupted your rate hike cycle, and you interrupted your peso \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation, clearly the markets are going to demand a higher policy risk on the (country's yield) curve," said Siobhan Morden, head of Latin America research and strategy at RBS Securities.\par \par \uc2 Morden says her favorite investment in Chile is the long two-year break-even inflation trade. Break-even inflation is the difference between the nominal yield on a fixed-rate investment and the real yield on an inflation-linked investment of similar maturity and credit quality.\par \par \uc2 Rates on that trade jumped to around 3.65 percent on Tuesday from 3.55 percent in the previous session and are poised to rise further, Morden said.\par \par \uc2 * Stocks\par \par \uc2 Chilean stocks in general should benefit from an expected pause in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  monetary tightening cycle, which analysts see as a complementary measure to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation.\par \par \uc2 Miners should post a good performance as the global outlook for commodities remains positive.\par \par \uc2 "Companies related to the exporting sector and with regional exposure should boost the local stock market," Santiago-based brokerage BCI said in a report.\par \par \uc2 Chile's blue-chip IPSA index <.IPSA> rose 0.9 percent on Tuesday while the broader IGPA index <.IGPA> gained about 0.8 percent.\par \par \uc2 SELL\par \par \uc2 * Peso\par \par \uc2 The peso <CLP=> sank about 4.5 percent on Tuesday, to 487.60 per U.S. dollar, following the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcement. It is poised to weaken a little further before stabilizing at weaker levels and eventually resuming its appreciation trend, especially if commodity prices remain strong.\par \par \uc2 Most analysts say the peso could weaken to near 500.00 per dollar in the short term. Many see attractive entry points around that level, however.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  house view is bullish on commodities and copper in particular. If that outlook proves to be right, sellers of USD/CLP may surface if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trades above the 500 level," \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  analyst Felipe Q. Pianetti wrote in a research note.\par \par \uc2 * LONG-DATED BONDS\par \par \uc2 Chile's domestic yield curve is expected to become steeper as inflation expectations rise and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells more bonds to sterilize its dollar purchases.\par \par \uc2 Yields on Chile's peso-denominated bonds maturing in 2020 <CL00001265=RRPS> rose 36 basis points to 6.458 percent, according to Reuters data. (Additional reporting by Brad Haynes in Santiago; Editing by Leslie Adler)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CHILE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BUY OR SELL)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|U|M|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110104e7140012q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
