\par\par \b \uc2 TEXT-Chile  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  to buy $12 bln to help tame peso\b0\par\par\uc2 579 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2011\par 01:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Jan 3 (Reuters) - The Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and purchase $12 billion in 2011 to tame the strong peso's impact on the local economy.\par \par \uc2 Following is the text of the announcement:\par \par \uc2 "The board of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Chile\uc2  has decided to initiate a program to buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen its international liquidity position. The aim of this initiative is to raise international reserves to a level compatible with those in economies similar to \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's. Moreover, this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should soften the impact of exchange rate adjustment in our economy.\par \par \uc2 "Global risks are heightened. The international economy is in an unusual position, characterized by high commodity prices, low interest rates, a slow recovery in developed economies and the depreciation of the U.S. dollar. Meanwhile, emerging economies are growing strongly and their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are appreciating. Significant risks include an escalation of financial tensions in Europe, sustained high rates of unemployment in developed economies and severe adjustments in emerging economies facing inflationary pressures. The availability of additional reserves will allow a better handling of any major deterioration of the global outlook."\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets are under stress and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  adjustments occur asymmetrically. There is also the risk that the uncoupling of global growth could continue beyond expectations, which could intensify \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tensions. Therefore the effects of this measure, although transitory, should provide room to allow real adjustments in the national economy."\par \par \uc2 "To implement this program, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Chile\uc2  will accumulate additional international reserves worth $12 billion in 2011 through regular dollar purchases from Jan. 5 until the end of December 2011. This program will bring the international liquidity position of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 17 percent of GDP."\par \par \uc2 "The monetary effects of this measure will be offset in order to maintain peso liquidity at levels consistent with current monetary policy. This sterilization will be achieved with a combination of short-term liquidity instruments and long-term debt issuance, according to the annual calendar that will be announced promptly. The first phase of this program, effective from Jan. 5 to Feb. 9, will consist of daily purchases of $50 million through competitive auctions. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Chile\uc2  will promptly communicate the next steps, which may be revised depending on market conditions."\par \par \uc2 "The accumulation of international reserves implies significant financial costs associated with the difference between the return on investment and the cost of financing. The proposed level of international reserves is consistent with the long-term financial sustainability of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although there is limited room in this regard."\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board reiterates its commitment to conducting monetary policy based on an inflation target and floating exchange rate. For a country like Chile, which may face significant changes in foreign financial conditions and terms of trade, exchange rate flexibility is an essential ingredient of macroeconomic and financial stability. On the contrary, rigid exchange rate arrangements may have undesirable costs on the volatility of growth, credit, interest rates and inflation. In a volatile environment as seen in recent years, an inflation targeting and floating exchange rate regime has shown its benefits in allowing a more stable evolution of the Chilean economy. Furthermore, our floating regime allows \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in emergency situations, such as the one announced in this press release."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CHILE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CENBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 -TEXT|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110104e7140000v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
