\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  peso slumps on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 ;real recovers\b0\par\par\uc2 677 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2011\par 21:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 (Repeats to additional subscribers)\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso closes down 4.5 pct at 9-week low\par \par \uc2 * Brazilian real pares losses after press conference\par \par \uc2 * Finance Minister Guido Mantega announces no new measures\par \par \uc2 * Mexico eschews \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , benefiting peso (Adds comments from Mexico, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Brad Haynes\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/SANTIAGO, Jan 4 (Reuters) - Chile's peso suffered its biggest daily drop in more than 25 years on Tuesday on tough new \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans while the Brazilian real recovered after Brasilia stopped short of introducing further measures.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=> slumped as much as 4.9 percent to 489.60 per dollar. It later closed 4.5 percent down at a 9-week low of 487.60 -- its biggest daily loss since February 1985, according to daily \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real <BRBY> also weakened sharply after the government announced it would hold a news conference in the afternoon to tackle \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues, prompting speculation fresh measures could be announced.\par \par \uc2 But Finance Minister Guido Mantega said very little and only reiterated that the government was ready to act, causing the real immediately to pare losses.\par \par \uc2 Chile has taken one of the most hands-off approaches in Latin America to its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. But it surprised investors late on Monday with a massive dollar-buying plan.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced it will buy $12 billion to tame the peso, which has appreciated more than 17 percent against the greenback since the end of June. For details, see [ID:nN03137860].\par \par \uc2 Like many attractive emerging economies across Latin America and Asia, Chile has struggled with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation that has made its exports more difficult to sell abroad and flooded the country with cheap imports. <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Graphic on region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/cat64r"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/cat64r}}}\uc2  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's surprise move added to existing concerns about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the region as it could give countries such as Brazil an excuse to implement more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures.\par \par \uc2 "If the pretty conservative Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 , what can you expect of the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 !" said Pedro Tuesta, senior Latin America economist at research firm 4Cast Inc in Washington.\par \par \uc2 However, others played down a possible regional impact.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  is just the last domino to fall into \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . I don't think it changes others' attitudes as they are already \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Tony Volpon, head of emerging markets research for the Americas at Nomura in New York.\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL: KING OF \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real pared its losses to close 0.79 percent weaker at 1.662 per dollar on the local spot market, after closing at its strongest level since Sept. 1 2008 in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's trade and industry minister said on Monday the country would not remain "passive" while the real continues to strengthen.\par \par \uc2 Latin America's biggest economy has already taken the lead in the region when it comes to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , buying vast amounts of dollars on a daily basis and raising taxes on inflows. But investors worry the government could increase those levies even further and take other measures, such as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the futures market. For possible measures, see [ID:nN01117570].\par \par \uc2 Mexico is now the only major Latin American country that is not heavily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, partly because the peso is fully convertible and thus more widely traded and harder to control.\par \par \uc2 The country has also suffered more from the financial crisis, which means it has not seen the flood of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -boosting investment experienced by Chile and Brazil.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso <MXN=> gained 0.14 percent to 12.2318 per dollar, even as U.S. stocks were mixed.\par \par \uc2 "If you believe that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Mexico is pretty moderate and subtle, then the peso become more attractive in the eyes of investors," said Luis Flores, an economist at brokerage IXE in Mexico City. (Additional reporting by Jean Luis Arce in Mexico City; Editing by Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)(REPEAT)|LANGEN|ABN|D|E|RBN|M|U|RNP|DNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110107e714001g3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
