\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks End 1.3% Higher; Some Companies Get Boost From  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 577 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2011\par 21:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's blue-chip Ipsa index ended 1.3% higher Tuesday, as exporters got a boost from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's planned purchase of $12 billion aimed at stemming the peso's appreciation.\par \par \uc2 After settlement, the Ipsa was 1.2% higher on the day at 5024.66, just shy of a record high. Meanwhile, volume slipped to 203.6 billion Chilean pesos ($417.4 million) from CLP498.8 billion the prior session.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move to increase foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves by $12 billion this year will help exporters, who have been sent reeling as the peso's appreciation in recent months cut into the competitiveness of their products abroad.\par \par \uc2 Wine exporter and producer Vina Concha Y Toro (VCO, CONCHATOR.SN) jumped 1.8% to CLP1,150.00, while \uc2 Coca-Cola\uc2  bottler and beverage company \uc2 Embotelladora Andina\uc2  (AKOB, ANDINA-B.SN) gained 3.3% to CLP1,961.70.\par \par \uc2 "A company like Concha y Toro sees sales in dollars and costs in pesos, so a move like this obviously benefits the company," said Ximena Garcia, deputy director of studies at local brokerage EuroAmerica.\par \par \uc2 Commodities-related companies, which export the majority of their products, also posted gains.\par \par \uc2 Fertilizer and specialty chemical producer SQM's (SQM) more liquid B-series (SQM-B.SN) advanced 1.0% to CLP27,963.00; integrated steel and iron-ore producer Cap (CAP.SN) gained 1.2% to CLP25,962.00; pulp and paper producer CMPC (CMPC.SN) rose 2.1% to CLP25,300.00; and fuel and forestry conglomerate Copec (COPEC.SN), the most heavily weighted share on the Ipsa, jumped 1.9% to CLP9,299.20.\par \par \uc2 "A cheaper peso, helps exporters boost their bottom lines," said Rodrigo Mujica, analyst with local brokerage BCI Corridor de Bolsa.\par \par \uc2 Construction and real-estate companies again posted strong gains on expectations that a ramping up of post-earthquake reconstruction activity this year will boost profits.\par \par \uc2 Construction company Besalco (BESALCO.SN), which was incorporated into the Ipsa index on Monday, leaped 5.8% to CLP1,085.70, and real-estate developer \uc2 Socovesa\uc2  (SOCOVESA.SN) gained 2.8% to CLP383.06.\par \par \uc2 In other market news, the peso ended 4.8% weaker versus the dollar as the market digested the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP487.80 to the dollar, versus Monday's close of CLP465.40, which was a 32-month high. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a range of CLP482.70 to CLP490.50\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's long-awaited \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pulled the peso sharply lower. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "exceptional" and carries credibility, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jose De Gregorio told reporters.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended sharply higher after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  detailed plans to use $2 billion in short-term instruments and facilities and $10 billion in both peso-denominated and inflation-indexed bonds to "sterilize" its dollar purchases.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.80%, up from 2.67% on Monday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 3.11%, up from 2.95% the previous session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 04-01-11 2050GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5057   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110104e7140012x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
