\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Says  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Exceptional; Peso Weakens\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito and Charles Roth   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 737 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2011\par 20:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program is an "exceptional measure" and as such carries credibility, the bank's president, Jose De Gregorio, said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The market evidently agreed, knocking the peso down nearly 5% against the U.S. dollar by the end of the first full trading session following the program's announcement late Monday. The plan to accumulate $12 billion in additional international reserves is the largest since the peso's free float was adopted in the late 1990s, De Gregorio noted.\par \par \uc2 The peso has been trading at 32-month highs against the dollar in recent months, prompting exporters to demand a lifeline as the strong local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  cuts into the competitiveness of their products. Yet the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Chile\uc2  has resisted far longer than peers in emerging markets from South Korea to Thailand, Taiwan, Colombia and Brazil in purchasing dollars, applying capital controls, or increasing local banks' reserve requirements in bids to cool red-hot local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and heated domestic demand.\par \par \uc2 "We haven't fallen into the addiction of repetitive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," De Gregorio told reporters. He predicted that the size of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will make it effective "in softening the pressures on the peso."\par \par \uc2 The peso ended local trade Tuesday 4.8% weaker at CLP487.80 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "We now finally have some breathing room," said Antonio Walker, president of the Fedefruta fruit exporters trade group. The strong peso had "paralyzed" exporters, he said, noting that it reduced their incomes and made it difficult to cover their costs and invest.\par \par \uc2 At least in the short-term, economists said, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's plan should prove effective.\par \par \uc2 "We expect a meaningful impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The bank has gained a lot of credibility over the past decade regarding its commitment to a free-floating exchange regime... and we think this has enhanced the effectiveness of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a policy tool," \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 This is the fourth time the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market since eliminating the peso's trading bands in 1999 and letting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  float freely, and the first time since 2008.\par \par \uc2 This bout of dollar buying won't affect Chile's long-term competitiveness, nor its long-term real exchange rate, De Gregorio insisted.\par \par \uc2 Much, however, depends on the global backdrop.\par \par \uc2 "The bigger picture is that emerging markets have relatively good fundamentals [and have to deal] with domestic inflation pressures against a backdrop of strong capital inflows, which push up the values of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Neil Shearing, Latin American economist at Capital Economics in London.\par \par \uc2 De Gregorio pointed out that Chile hasn't seen net capital inflows. "Today the problem isn't a massive inflow of capital," he said.\par \par \uc2 Still, record-high copper prices, the wide differentials between interest rates in Chile and rock-bottom rates across the developed world, and a rapidly expanding Chilean economy suggest the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program can't guarantee the peso won't resume appreciation.\par \par \uc2 Chile is the world's biggest copper exporter, so sustained high demand out of China and other high-growth emerging markets implies continued high prices for the red metal, and more pressure on Chile's peso.\par \par \uc2 "If the terms of trade continue to improve, the U.S. dollar continues to weaken in global markets, and the Chilean economy's cyclical position remains markedly strong vis-a-vis the trading partners, we sense the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not lean excessively against the wind of further moderate Chilean peso strength," \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  economist Alberto Ramos said.\par \par \uc2 But given the size of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, which involves an initial $50 million in daily "very predictable non-discretionary" dollar purchases, Ramos said it "stands a good chance of being effective."\par \par \uc2 Moreover, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can also continue with interest rate increases, reining in domestic demand and inflationary pressures. That, in turn, should help ease pressure on the peso.\par \par \uc2 De Gregorio said the bank remains committed to a target of 3% inflation in a two-year policy horizon. January-November inflation for 2010 stood at 2.9%.\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito and Charles Roth, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 -Anjali Cordeiro and Carolina Pica contributed to this report. [ 04-01-11 1930GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110104e7140012h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppi