\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Exporters Applaud  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 , Request Govt Measures\b0\par\par\uc2 395 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2011\par 20:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exporters applauded the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but asked for the government to follow up with other measures to help boost the competitiveness of their sector.\par \par \uc2 With the peso trading at or near a 32-month high against the dollar in recent months, exporters clamored for a lifeline as the strength of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hurt the competitiveness of their products abroad.\par \par \uc2 Chile's export-dependent economy is among the world leaders in the production of natural resources such as copper, fertilizers, molybdenum, wood pulp, fresh fruit and wines.\par \par \uc2 "[The exchange rate] paralyzed us. It reduced our income, made it difficult to pay our business costs and froze our investments, creating debt [in the sector]. We now finally have some breathing room," said Antonio Walker, president of the Fedefruta fruit exporters trade group.\par \par \uc2 The breathing room created by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's program to increase foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves by $12 billion in 2011, however, may be short-lived if the government doesn't follow up with measures of its own, exporters argue.\par \par \uc2 The government needs to "take long-term complementary measures to protect products made in \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 's impact isn't diluted over time by factors such as increasing copper prices," said Roberto Fantuzzi, the president of Chile's Asexma exporters trade group.\par \par \uc2 As Chile is the world's premier copper producer, accounting for nearly a third of global supply, the peso often takes trading cues from the metal's international prices. Record-high copper prices, on strong fundamentals, helped to fuel the peso's rise in recent months.\par \par \uc2 Among other initiatives, Asexma is calling for long-term \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedging programs "for investment projects in the non-commodities export sector."\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day, Finance Minister Felipe Larrain said that the government "supported and appreciated" the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move, pointing out that the ministry and the autonomous \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  closely coordinate their measures.\par \par \uc2 According to Larrain, the government will continue with its own measures to help stem the peso's strength. These include limiting fiscal spending, holding dollar financing at a minimum, improving financial legislation and cutting red tape for exporters.\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 04-01-11 1926GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110104e7140012g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
