\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Ends 4.8% Weaker On $12B  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Announcement\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 391 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2011\par 17:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The Chilean peso ended 4.8% weaker versus the dollar Tuesday as the market digested the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by increasing its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves by $12 billion this year.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP487.80 to the dollar, versus Monday's close of CLP465.40, which was a 32-month high. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a range of CLP482.70 to CLP490.50\par \par \uc2 Exporters had demanded a lifeline in recent months, as the strength of the peso hurt the competitiveness of their products abroad.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's long-awaited \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pulled the peso sharply lower because as the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "exceptional", it carries credibility, the bank's President Jose De Gregorio told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Many analysts, however, question the mid-to-long-term effectiveness of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  considering historically high copper prices, the wide interest rate differential between Chile and the U.S. and a rapidly recovering Chilean economy versus sluggish growth in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Over the next several sessions it is likely that the peso will weaken to levels near CLP500, "at which point the market will again look at fundamentals such as [international] copper prices, economic activity, interest rates and how the dollar evolves against its [major rivals], to get direction for the future of the Chilean peso," said local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chile.\par \par \uc2 As Chile is the world's premier copper producer accounting for nearly a third of global supply, the peso often takes trading cues from the metal's international prices.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended vastly higher after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  detailed plans to use $2 billion in short-term instruments and facilities and $10 billion in both peso-denominated and inflation-indexed bonds to "sterilize" its $12 billion dollar purchasing program.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.80%, from 2.67% on Monday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 3.11%, from 2.95% the previous session\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 04-01-11 1655GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110104e714000yh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
