\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Chile Intervention \highlight\uc2  To Have Meaningful Impact - \uc2 Barclays\b0\par\par\uc2 1,164 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2011\par 17:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Robert Flint, 212-416-2216; \par robert.flint@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1614 GMT [Dow Jones] "We like buying USD/CLP on dips targeting 515," said Roberto Melzi, emerging markets analyst with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2 , in a research note. USD/CLP has risen about 5% to 488.20 versus Monday's close of 465.40, according to data provided by local newswire Valor Futuro. "We expect the announced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  package to have a meaningful effect on USD/CLP...In fact, we have revised our three-month forecast to 515, from 480, and do not discard some over-shooting in the near term, given unsupportive technicals," said Melzi. Chile's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will increase its foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves by $12 billion this year, as a way to soften the peso's sharp appreciation over the last several months. (anthony.esposito@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1549 GMT [Dow Jones] CAD is retreating, with USD/CAD hitting a session high at 0.9999, according to CQG, as oil dips below $89 a barrel. The faltering rally in oil is at least temporarily clipping CAD's wings, bringing it back to the parity zone after the earlier the strength that pushed USD to a session low at 0.9916. (don.curren@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1548 GMT [Dow Jones] Gilts fall Tuesday, as gains in equity markets and strong economic data damp demand for low yielding government debt. Having been shut on Monday, UK financial markets played catch up, with the FTSE rising by more than 2%. Already fading expectations of the BOE reviving quantitative easing were meanwhile knocked further after data showed UK manufacturing activity expanding at its fastest pace in 16 years. March gilts fall 0.69 at 118.80 and the 10-year gilt is down at 110.015, yielding 3.464%. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1547 GMT [Dow Jones] Traders of interest-rate futures seem focused squarely on arrival of December's FOMC minutes later Tuesday, as unexpected bump in factory orders is the latest economic report to generate a collective shrug. Many contracts prices remain higher in midmorning trade, indicating expectations that key rates will hold lower in the months ahead, bucking the positive economic data. Quarterly 2012 Eurodollar futures gain 1 to 4.5 basis points, though most 2011 contracts flat. Mar 10-yr note futures 7/32 higher at 120-12+, while Mar classic bond futures up 1/32 at 121-17. (jacob.bunge@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1530 GMT [Dow Jones] The euro's gains against the dollar have evaporated. The euro is now trading lower for the day against the dollar, having steadily retreated after a surprisingly strong report on November US factory orders. EUR/USD is at 1.3345, according to EBS via CQG, from 1.3353 late Monday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (stephen.bernard@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1528 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2  has reiterated its 'overweight' recommendation on \f28 \uc2 \f2 General Electric Capital Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 , saying GECC is undervalued in light of its unique support arrangement with industrial giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 General Electric\f28 \uc2 \f2 . In the wake of the Dodd-Frank bill, U.S. financials will no longer have the kind of outside support they have had access to until now, putting GECC in a favorable position, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2  said. The firm predicts GE's loan loss provisions will come down nearly 50% from 2009 numbers and that GECC bond issuance will come down to 2.7% of the credit markets from its peak of 4.3% in 2008. (katy.burne@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1526 GMT [Dow Jones] After studying the movements of 11 major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and gold, oil and copper over three and six month time frames, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brown Brothers Harriman\f28 \uc2 \f2  found CAD was most highly correlated with oil prices. In the past three months the correlation stands at 0.74, the highest in the BBH report, while over the past six months it's 0.645. AUD is in second place, with 0.635 and 0.615 respectively. "Outside of the past three months with Canadian dollar and oil (0.74), the other correlations we found, while interesting, are still too low and unstable to offer a good proxy to acquire or hedge commodity exposures," BBH said. (don.curren@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1524 GMT [Dow Jones] Communications company \f28 \uc2 \f2 CommScope, Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (CTV) is offering $1.5 billion of senior notes due 2018 as part of its LBO at the hands of \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Carlyle Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the largest of a trio of junk bond deals in the market so far Tuesday. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Charter Communications, Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is offering $750 million of senior unsecured notes due 2019 to repay bank debt, and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Regal Entertainment\f28 \uc2 \f2  is shopping a $100 mln add-on offering to its 9.125% notes due 2018. The Charter and Regal deals are expected to price Tuesday, while the \f28 \uc2 \f2 CommScope\f28 \uc2 \f2  offer is seen pricing next week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (michael.aneiro@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1523 GMT [Dow Jones] The dollar, at Y82.16, is crowding daily resistance at Y82.36. See chart at\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/5190"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/5190}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 A move above resistance, which is likely, would point the dollar up to Y83.31. But a move below Y81.77 would signal dollar buyers to take profits.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (stephen.cox@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1519 GMT [Dow Jones] Chile's peso was 5% against the dollar after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  announced late Monday that it will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market by increasing its foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves by $12 billion this year. As the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is "exceptional" it carries credibility, which explains why the peso fell so sharply, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's president Jose De Gregorio told reporters on Tuesday. USD/CLP was recently at 488.50 versus Monday's close of 465.40. (anthony.esposito@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1519 GMT [Dow Jones] The build up of structural short USD/JPY positions over recent years has reached extreme levels, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Many of these shorts are Japanese investors, particularly life companies hedging their extensive U.S. Treasury portfolios, likely to the tune of around USD 2.5 trillion. BNP says the anticipated change in global liquidity dynamics over the coming year and overall yield differentials and yield-curve dynamics provide the environment for position unwinding, with only a moderate adjustment to hedge ratios having a significant impact on USD/JPY. To position for this, BNP suggests a USD/JPY call with a strike at 110.00. USD/JPY now at 82.18. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1512 GMT [Dow Jones] The outlook for US corporate bonds is positive as corporations have paid down a lot of their debt and largely recovered from the financial crisis, says Fitch Ratings in a new report. While there is temptation for corporates to pursue shareholder friendly activities and there are lingering macro economic fears, better market liquidity and the cash cushion corporates are sitting on should help them expand their businesses in 2011, Fitch said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (katy.burne@dowjones.com) [ 01-04-11 1114ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110104e714000ac\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
