\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Slides 5% After  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Announcement\b0\par\par\uc2 1,161 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2011\par 16:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Robert Flint, 212-416-2216; \par robert.flint@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1519 GMT [Dow Jones] Chile's peso was 5% against the dollar after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  announced late Monday that it will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market by increasing its foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves by $12 billion this year. As the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is "exceptional" it carries credibility, which explains why the peso fell so sharply, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's president Jose De Gregorio told reporters on Tuesday. USD/CLP was recently at 488.50 versus Monday's close of 465.40. (anthony.esposito@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1519 GMT [Dow Jones] The build up of structural short USD/JPY positions over recent years has reached extreme levels, says \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 . Many of these shorts are Japanese investors, particularly life companies hedging their extensive U.S. Treasury portfolios, likely to the tune of around USD 2.5 trillion. BNP says the anticipated change in global liquidity dynamics over the coming year and overall yield differentials and yield-curve dynamics provide the environment for position unwinding, with only a moderate adjustment to hedge ratios having a significant impact on USD/JPY. To position for this, BNP suggests a USD/JPY call with a strike at 110.00. USD/JPY now at 82.18. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1512 GMT [Dow Jones] The outlook for US corporate bonds is positive as corporations have paid down a lot of their debt and largely recovered from the financial crisis, says Fitch Ratings in a new report. While there is temptation for corporates to pursue shareholder friendly activities and there are lingering macro economic fears, better market liquidity and the cash cushion corporates are sitting on should help them expand their businesses in 2011, Fitch said.\par \par \uc2 (katy.burne@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1511 GMT [Dow Jones] Dollar ekes out gains after news that US factory orders rose unexpectedly in November. The data is likely to add to perceptions that the US economy is on firmer footing and feed risk appetite. The euro was at $1.3357 from $1.3353 late Monday, according to EBS via CQG. The dollar was a Y82.16 from Y81.73. (javier.david@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1504 GMT [Dow Jones] Tsys are heading a tad lower after factory orders data, which was better than expected. 2-yr flat to 0.609% and 10-yr off 4/32 to 3.354%. 3-yr is lagging, off 18/32 to 4.437%. (deborah.blumberg@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1502 GMT [Dow Jones] US factory orders unexpectedly rise 0.7% in November. Economists had forecast a 0.1% decline. Non-defense capital goods orders excluding aircraft increased 2.6% in November, after falling 3.2% the month before. Those orders are considered an indicator of capital spending by businesses. The latest ISM and regional Fed reports show the factory sectory is leading US recovery.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (kathleen.madigan@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1458 GMT [Dow Jones] Dollar firm ahead of US factory orders data, which analysts expect to show a 0.1% decline in November. Better-than-expected economic data has fed risk appetite that tends to undermine the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . However, some analysts believe constructive U.S. data will ultimately support the greenback. Recent data also shows traders are relatively short dollars, which could lead to upward pressure on the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . EUR/USD gives up European session gains to trade around 1.3375, USD/JPY at top of day's range near 82.20.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (javier.david@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1451 GMT [Dow Jones] Sterling's interest rate advantage over both the USD and EUR is growing, notes Citi. The bank says the 2-year GBP-USD rate differential suggests that GBP/USD should be trading closer to 1.60 than its current level of 1.56. It's the same story in EUR/GBP where 2-year rate differentials have tightened over the last two weeks with euro yields slipping while GBP yields rise; a similar comparison between \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot and rate spreads points to more upside in GBP/JPY, says the bank. GBP/JPY now trades at 128.30, EUR/GBP 0.8575 and GBP/USD 1.5598. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1450 GMT [Dow Jones] Tsys continue to bounce around unchanged Tuesday as the market gears up for factory orders data; the exception is 30-yr, which is underperforming. Drop of just 0.1% expected for factory orders vs 0.9% fall in the prior month. Better than expected data would likely push Tsy ylds up. 2-yr flat to 0.605%, 10-yr off 1/32 to 3.342%. 30-yr off 11/32 to yield 4.421%. (deborah.blumberg@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1446 GMT [Dow Jones] Polish Treasury bonds continue to weaken, still in the aftermath of proposed changes to pension system, forecasted CPI acceleration in December, traders say. That's why Wednesday auction of up to PLN6.5 billion in 2- and 5-year papers will be a serious test to the market, they add. "I see higher yields, investors will want higher risk premium," a local trader says. Average yield on 2-year bonds is at 4.87% from 4.84% late Monday, 5-year at 5.60% from 5.54%, 10-year at 6.14% from 6.11%. (malgorzata.halaba@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1438 GMT [Dow Jones] The big rallies in the Japanese yen and Swiss franc last month could quickly reverse themselves in January, says Citi's strategists. Citi says the yen and franc were used heavily in December to fund carry trades and as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose last month, traders had to cover their short positions. If trades are rolled off or sold, Citi says "we could see a sizeable catch-up sell off" in January. The yen and franc are both losing ground to the dollar Tuesday. USD/JPY is up to 82.14 from 81.73 late Monday, according to EBS via CQG. USD/CHF is up to 0.9446 from 0.9343.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (stephen.bernard@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 14:34 GMT [Dow Jones] The U.K. pound is doing a 180-degree turn from Monday's sharp selloff, thanks to better-than-expected U.K. manufacturing and mortgage data. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2  notes in a research report that sterling is "the best performing G10 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 " in Tuesday's trading. Growing interest in risk assets is also helping the British \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the bank said, adding that it "should continue to benefit from more evidence that its rate advantage over USD and EUR is growing." Given the rate differentials and economic fundamentals of the British economy, "GBPUSD should be trading closer to $1.60 than $1.55," Citi said. GBP/USD up more than 1% on the day at 1.5617.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (javier.david@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  David Biderman, 212-416-4437; \par david.biderman@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 01-04-11 1019ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110104e7140009q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
