\par\par \b \uc2 INSTANT VIEW 3- \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  to curb peso gains\b0\par\par\uc2 505 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2011\par 22:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Jan 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced on Monday a plan to purchase as much as $12 billion in 2011 to stem the appreciation of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the peso.\par \par \uc2 The peso <CLP=> on Monday firmed almost 0.5 percent to 465.5 per dollar to close at its strongest level since May 2008.\par \par \uc2 For a story, see [ID:nN03137860].\par \par \uc2 Following are comments from analysts:\par \par \uc2 MARJORIE HERNANDEZ, LATIN AMERICA \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  ANALYST, \uc2 HSBC\uc2 , NEW YORK:\par \par \uc2 "I think the market was anticipating some sort of reaction. The question was at what level. There was a little bit of a divergence in views as to whether it should come below the 460 or 465 level. But clearly this was entering a danger zone.\par \par \uc2 "When you look at the press release, clearly it is more a medium-term concern that the underlying pressures that have been driving emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  stronger are here to stay for 2011. They do talk about a divergence between emerging markets and developed markets and they do allude to higher commodity prices.\par \par \uc2 "A lot of commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were rallying and Chile was among them. Now that the announcement has been made I think that you can start to look at Chile underperforming the rest of the commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Volumes in Chile are OK, they are not as high and I think $50 million does make a difference."\par \par \uc2 MATIAS MADRID, CHIEF ECONOMIST, BANCO PENTA, SANTIAGO:\par \par \uc2 "This was definitely a surprise. It was expected around 460 pesos per dollar, so this came a little early.\par \par \uc2 "Obviously, this will have an immediate impact on the exchange rate, which should rise to around 480 pesos per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "This is quite an aggressive measure, a strong play by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The most important thing is the volume of the purchases, which is quite high."\par \par \uc2 "It won't be enough to entirely settle the issue. If copper keeps advancing toward $4.50 per pound we can expect it to come back. But this should have a short-term effect."\par \par \uc2 ALBERTO RAMOS, SENIOR ECONOMIST, GOLDMAN SACHS, NEW YORK:\par \par \uc2 "I think it will have some impact, but not a major one because even the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  admits that part of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pressure stems from fundamental factors, such as a world with asymmetrical growth levels between emerging markets and developed economies.\par \par \uc2 "We'll have some impact, but (it won't be that large) if we continue to see commodity prices rallying and a weak dollar in the global economy. The idea is not to reverse the trend (of peso appreciation), but probably to smooth it a little bit."\par \par \uc2 EDUARDO SUAREZ, EMERGING MARKETS ANALYST, RBC CAPITAL MARKETS\par \par \uc2 "Although the announcement could present some short-term headwinds, we believe fundamentals are still supportive for the Chilean peso." (Reporting by Walter Brandimarte and Daniel Bases in New York, Brad Haynes in Santiago)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CHILE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CENBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (INSTANT VIEW,UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|E|RBN|D|M   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110103e713000xq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\