\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil real, Chile peso pass 2 year highs\b0\par\par\uc2 634 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2011\par 14:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real, Mexican peso gain 0.9 pct\par \par \uc2 * Chilean peso firms to strongest since May 2008\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unveils \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan\par \par \uc2 (Adds comments, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/MEXICO CITY, Jan 3 (Reuters) - Strong reports on global manufacturing drove Brazil's real and Chile's peso to more than 2 year highs on Monday and Chilean authorities said they would start buying dollars to curb the peso's strength.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso hit a six-week high after data showed the manufacturing sector in the United States grew for a 17th straight month in December, boding well for Mexican factories that are closely tied to U.S. output. For details, see [ID:nN03175600]\par \par \uc2 European factory data was also solid as was an output survey in China, Brazil's top trading partner. Slower growth and cooling inflation seen in the Chinese data eased concerns of an interest rate hike by the world's second biggest economy. [ID:nTOE6BU02S]\par \par \uc2 "This implies that Chinese authorities will refrain from taking aggressive measures and not slow down their economy too much," said Emilio Diez De Sollano, an analyst at brokerage Monex in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 Investors are concerned that Chinese rate hikes could weigh on Latin American growth. Asian countries, especially China, have been consuming Latin American commodities such as Brazilian soybeans and Chilean copper.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=> firmed almost 0.5 percent to 465.5 per dollar to close at its strongest since May 2008.\par \par \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said late on Monday it would take similar measures to control the peso's strength as countries like Brazil and Colombia have implemented to protect local exporters from sharp gains in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 After the local market had closed, Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would start buying $50 million a day in dollars in a bid to slow peso appreciation.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <MXN=> strengthened 0.9 percent to 12.2551 per dollar in its biggest one-day percentage gain since Oct. 20.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had soaked up 592 million dollars by exercising dollar put options that Mexico implemented early in 2010 to build up its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 REAL JUMPS ON DILMA'S FIRST DAY\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> bid 0.9 percent stronger at 1.649 per U.S. dollar on the local spot market on Monday, closing at its strongest since Sept. 1, 2008.\par \par \uc2 The new government of President Dilma Rousseff vowed on Monday to push for budget cuts to tackle rising inflation that is one of the biggest threats to Brazil's booming economy. [ID:nN03270814]\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to hike interest rates later this month, which will likely entice more investors to buy high-yielding Brazilian debt.\par \par \uc2 "Investors are betting that Brazil will receive more money in the coming months. In this context, there is no way the real is getting weaker," said Ovidio Soares, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at the Interbolsa brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 But further gains may be limited, analysts cautioned.\par \par \uc2 After sharp gains during most of the past decade, the real may not offer as much value as other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region, according to some analysts. Investors have also been put off by authorities' efforts to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains via dollar purchases, tax increases and frequent verbal warnings.\par \par \uc2 The real's recent surge is raising concerns that authorities could step up efforts to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength.\par \par \uc2 Trade and Industry Minister Fernando Pimentel said on Monday that Brazil's new government "will not stay passive" as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthens. [ID:nN03181487\}\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|RNP|PCM   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110106e713000tv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
