\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Ends At 32-Mo High On Record Copper; \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Seen Nearer\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 428 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2011\par 17:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso ended at a 32-month high against the dollar as international copper prices hit a new record, bringing the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closer to levels expected to prompt \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The peso finished stronger at CLP465.40 to the dollar compared with Thursday's close of CLP467.30, while trading in a range of CLP465.10 to CLP467.00.\par \par \uc2 Markets and banks in Chile were closed Friday for the New Year's Eve holiday.\par \par \uc2 After appreciating 7.8% in 2010 versus the dollar, the peso continued to strengthen in the new year as international copper prices rose to a record high.\par \par \uc2 As Chile is the world's premier copper producer, accounting for nearly 35% of global output, the peso often takes cues from the metal's international prices.\par \par \uc2 In New York trading, the most actively traded contact, for March delivery, was recently up 0.5% at $4.4670 a pound, after setting a fresh intraday record at $4.4980, on strong fundamentals and declining inventories.\par \par \uc2 With the peso's sharp appreciation in recent months, exporters have demanded \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the strength of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hurts their competitiveness abroad.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently said it doesn't rule out increasing its foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves as a way to limit the peso's recent strength.\par \par \uc2 Traders see an increased risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the peso appreciates to CLP450-CLP460. Some traders, however, feel an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have limited effects because of historically high copper prices, broad international dollar weakness and strong economic growth in Chile compared to the sluggish U.S. recovery.\par \par \uc2 "A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may happen, there's political pressure for them to act, to help exporters. But market forces and fundamentals, such as record-high copper and robust growth in \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , may well erase the effect of an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in very little time," said Ronald Volpi, head \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with local brokerage EuroAmerica.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended higher in light over-the-counter trading.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.67%, from 2.65% on Thursday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.95%, from 2.89% the previous session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 03-01-11 1659GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110103e713000pf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
