\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Trading Stronger, Moves Toward  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Territory\b0\par\par\uc2 338 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2011\par 12:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Corrected January 3, 2011 07:53 ET (13:53 GMT) [ 03-01-11 1148GMT ]\par \par \uc2 (The headline "\b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  Peso Trading 2.4% Stronger, Moves Toward \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Territory," published at 6:48 a.m. EST and the story with the same headline published at 7:03 a.m. EST, misstated the percent change on the day. The correct version follows:)\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's peso was trading stronger against the dollar early Monday, at a 32-month high, moving closer toward levels thought to merit an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 In recent trading the peso gained to CLP465.00 to the dollar, versus Thursday's close of CLP467.30, while trading in a range of CLP465.00 to CLP467.00.\par \par \uc2 Markets and banks in Chile were closed Friday for the New Year's Eve holiday.\par \par \uc2 The peso appreciated 7.8% versus the dollar in 2010, prompting exporters to clamor for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the strength of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hurts their competitiveness abroad.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently said it doesn't rule out increasing its foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves as a way to limit the peso's recent strength.\par \par \uc2 Traders now see an increased risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the peso appreciates to CLP450-CLP460.\par \par \uc2 "It's very likely that the peso may strengthen to CLP460 and beyond this week, which is a range where the risk of [\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  increases greatly," said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader Cristobal Aviles with \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As Chile is the world's premier copper producer, accounting for nearly 35% of global output, the peso often takes cues from the metal's international prices. Spot copper in London gained 1.7% to an all-time high of $4.41776 on Friday, according to Chilean state copper commission Cochilco, on declining stocks and strong demand.\par \par \uc2 "Since the Chilean market was closed on Friday, it's playing catch-up today," said Aviles.\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 03-01-11 1251GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110103e713000hv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
