\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Flat On Threat Of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 1,337 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Dezember 2010\par 13:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1210 GMT [Dow Jones] Chile's peso is trading virtually flat versus the dollar on concerns about a possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said early last week it doesn't rule out increasing its foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves. With the peso trading at 31-month highs against the U.S. dollar, exporters have demanded \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as the strength of the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hurts the competitiveness of their products abroad. Traders see an increased risk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the peso gains to CLP460-CLP465. In recent trading the peso was at CLP469.70 to the dollar, versus Friday's close of CLP469.80, according to data provided by local newswire Valor Futuro. (anthony.esposito@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1206 GMT [Dow Jones] While the bigger picture for EUR/USD suggests the downside is favored, SEBanken says there are not enough leads to suggest a directional stance for Monday. EUR/USD trades at 1.3165 and the bank pegs resistance at 1.3185 and 1.3202, support at 1.3072 and 1.3055.(gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1205 GMT [Dow Jones] China's Christmas day rate hike was the second in less than 3 months and did not come as a big surprise says \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2 . The pace of rate hikes has so far been relatively aggressive however with only 3 more expected over the next year they are likely to be front-loaded in 1H of 2011 says the bank, with the PBOC on hold through most of the 2H as inflation again starts to ease. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1155 GMT [Dow Jones] With London markets closed and New York suffering from severe weather conditions trading is likely to be seriously curtailed as the day unfolds. The latest travel news for New York does not look promising with nearly all subway lines and both LIRR and most MTA North trains suspended. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1146 GMT [Dow Jones] Euro Overnight Index Average fixed at 0.396% Friday, up from 0.356% Thursday. Monday, the interbank overnight rate is trading higher between 0.35% and 0.40% vs 0.28% and 0.35% Thursday. The market has picked up from Thursday but it is still sluggish, traders say, adding that the market is concentrating on the overnight rate and tomorrow-next trades. Earlier Monday, 3-month Euribor fixed at 1.014%, unchanged from Friday. (michael.denzin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1136 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/GBP nudges up to a fresh one-week high of 0.8527. London markets are closed so trade in GBP/USD is extremely limited, however Europe is open and with EUR/USD trading at 5-day highs EUR/GBP is heading North. Next resistance for EUR/GBP is likely around 0.8552, its one-month high. GBP/USD now trades at 1.5447. EUR/USD at 1.3166. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1125 GMT [Dow Jones] \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market reaction in Asia to China's surprise Christmas Day 25 basis point rate hike is limited, notes \uc2 UBS\uc2 . USD initially strengthened against AUD but those gains were then surrendered. The bank says this does not suggest AUD has suddenly developed an immunity to policy tightening risks in China, rather that the absence of a stronger reaction probably has much more to do with thin year-end trading conditions. AUD/USD now trades at 1.0036 from Friday's 1.0043 close. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1058 GMT [Dow Jones] India government bonds are mildly higher, but are off session highs on profit-booking as traders view bonds, especially the most-traded note, may have touched their respective price resistances, prompting players to hold bets, a trader with a primary dealership says. The most-traded 8.13% 2022 bond is at 100.95 after rising to 101.10 intraday, compared with 100.87 last close. "Traders think the 8.13% 2022 bond has rallied quite a lot and if this note is part of RBI's bond buyback this week, traders may have to compromise because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not repurchase this bond at very low yields," the trader says. The 2022 bond yield is at 8.0%, off the intraday low of 7.98%. He notes, the tight liquidity situation among banks is also limiting gains in bonds. The RBI has scheduled up to INR120 billion of bond repurchases this week to ease a cash crunch. (khushita.vasant@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1047 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/INR is up as local shares fall and banks buy USD on behalf of oil importers to settle their month-end bills, a trader with a private bank says. The pair is at 45.24, a tad of the intraday high of 45.26 and compared with 45.12 late Friday. "The pair gained further strength as the Sensex turned negative. Oil bids will continue to support the pair during the last week of the month," the trader says. He tips the pair to trade in a 45.05-45.35 band during the week. The Sensex ends down 0.2% after rising as much as 0.6% intraday. (sourav.mishra@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1043 GMT [Dow Jones] India's overnight indexed swaps are mildly up in thin volume as market participants shrug off China's interest rate hike over the weekend and investors hold off from entering new positions due to the holiday season, a foreign bank trader says. The one-year OIS rate is at 7.06%/7.09% from 7.05%/7.08% late Friday and the five-year OIS is at 7.73%/7.75% from 7.71%/7.74% at last close. "India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been pretty aggressive throughout this year in increasing rates so there hasn't been much of an impact due to China's action. But traders will watch out for a possible increase in diesel prices this week, which should drive swap rates a little higher," the trader says, noting the market has more or less digested that RBI may be forced to raise rates next month on rising inflationary pressures. (khushita.vasant@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1031 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/INR forward premia remain steady as a moribund spot and a persistent cash crunch in the banking system throw up few cues for the forwards market, says a trader with a foreign bank. The one-year forward premium is at 2.385 from 2.38 late Friday. "One key risk to forward premia was the possibility that the cash crunch would ease, but we're seeing absolutely no signs of that so far," the trader says. He tips premia to remain in a 2.30-2.40 band for the rest of the week, with future movements to hinge on what direction the spot takes in the new year. (bijou.george@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1003 GMT [Dow Jones] Pakistan's benchmark KSE-100 index is up 0.5% at 11925.65, aided by gains in oil shares. The gains came "after the government agreed last week to reimburse against oil bills, which will help improve the financial health of these companies," says a local dealer. \uc2 Pakistan State Oil\uc2  (PSO.KA) received around PKR28.5 billion ($333 million) last week against fuel sales made to power companies purchasing oil to run their power plants. "The reimbursement doesn't cover the total dues, but is enough to ease liquidity worries of these companies," the dealer says. He adds, around PKR300 billion was outstanding between the oil marketing companies, refineries and gas companies before the payment was made. Foreign fund buying is also boosting sentiment as they pumped over $10 million into the local market last week. \uc2 Pakistan State Oil\uc2  (PSO.KA) is up 0.9% to PKR292.65 and Attock Refinery (ATRL.KA) is up 1.0% at PKR331.48. (zamir.haris@gmail.com) [ 12-27-10 0710ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101227e6cr0004x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
