\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Flat On Fear Of Possible  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 1,405 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Dezember 2010\par 13:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1248 GMT [Dow Jones] Chile's peso is virtually unchanged versus the dollar after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  upped the ante Monday by suggesting it could increase its foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves as a way to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. For months exporters have clamored for a lifeline as the peso's strength, trading just shy of a 31-month high, hampers the competitiveness of their products abroad. Traders see a real risk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the peso continues to appreciate to CLP460-CLP465. The rate is at 467.97 from a high of 469.46. (anthony.esposito@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1149 GMT [Dow Jones] The zloty is broadly steady in thin trade in absence of most investors and with the Warsaw Stock Exchange closed. EUR/PLN at 3.9656 from 3.9600 late Thursday, USD/PLN at 3.0219 from 3.0203. (marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1041 GMT [Dow Jones] Greece/10-year bund spread remains wide at 925 bps with trading thin and sporadic. "Greek spreads jumped about 25 bps on Thursday on unconfirmed reports that Greece is planning some form of debt repayment extension or default after 2013 which continues to spook the market," says a senior local trader. "On Friday we are barely seeing bid-ask bond pricing offers, so the cash market is in 'stand-still' despite widening 5-year CDS spreads. Activity isn't likely to return to normal levels until after the new year," he adds. Trading in the Greek bond market will close earlier than usual Friday at 1200 GMT. (nick.skrekas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1040 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/USD slips to the session low of 1.3110. The 200-day moving average at 1.3091 offers near-term support, says RBC. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1037 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/INR is lower in thin Christmas Eve trading, slightly pressured by gains in local stocks and possible USD selling by banks, a trader with a privately-run bank says. The pair is at 45.12 from 45.17 late Thursday. "Trading is pretty much lackluster with no decisive cues from the euro or other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as activity has tapered off in overseas markets on the festive weekend," the trader says, adding the EUR/USD and other risk \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are broadly rangebound despite Fitch's downgrade of Portugal late Thursday. He tips the pair in a 45.00-45.40 band for the rest of the year. The Sensex ends +0.5%. (khushita.vasant@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1027 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/INR forward premia are a tad higher, tracking a mild correction in the spot, but volumes aren't high enough to break the inverse spot-premia correlation, says a trader with a foreign bank. The one-year forward premium is at 2.385 from 2.37 late Thursday. But premia are looking a bit too high, and may be set to correct once volumes are back in full force in January, says the trader. He expects the gradual return of liquidity to the banking system in January to be the next key risk to long bets on premia. (bijou.george@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1010 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/INR implied volatilities are a tad lower as the onset of the holiday season dampens volumes and lowers the odds of a sharp swing in the spot until January, says a trader with a foreign bank. The one-month is trading at 8.10%/8.90% from 8.20%/8.90% late Thursday. "Holding gamma isn't typically very lucrative in this season," notes the trader. But he adds, the risk of a key global economic event such as a hitting the spot hard in an illiquid market is helping to prevent a sharper selloff on gamma. The one-week ATMF is currently at 6.50%/7.50% from 6.75%/7.75% late Thursday. (bijou.george@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0954 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai shares end up 0.1% at 1021.99 after trading in the doldrums. The SET Index wavered between negative and positive territories amid the absence of fresh drivers as traders operated in a holiday mode. The benchmark may ease early next week as some investors may not want to hold positions over the holiday season, says Somchai Anektaweepon. He tips support at the 1013-1015 zone and resistance is put at 1025. Telcos are higher on news state-owned \uc2 CAT Telecom\uc2 's board has approved \uc2 Total Access Communication\uc2  (DTAC.TH) and TrueMove, a unit of \uc2 True Corp\uc2 . (TRUE.TH), to establish additional cell sites to facilitate the trial of 3G mobile services. Among the most actively traded shares, \uc2 Total Access Communication\uc2  is up 3.6% at THB43.50, \uc2 True Corp\uc2 . is +0.8% at THB6.65, PTT (PTT.TH) is down 0.3% at THB318 and \uc2 PTT Exploration & Production\uc2  (PTTEP.TH) is down 1.2% at THB165. (piyarat.setthasiriphaiboon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0949 GMT [Dow Jones] The Sensex is +0.4% at 20,057.30 on thin volumes. "It is reassuring that markets have managed to hold on to gains despite subdued cues from global markets," says a local analyst. He adds, metals are seeing some buying interest "but otherwise there is little activity on account of the holiday season," says a local analyst. ITC (500875.BY) is leading gains and it's +1.7% at INR169.65 while \uc2 Larsen & Toubro\uc2  (500510.BY) is +1.1% at INR1,956.50. Among losers, \uc2 Tata Motors\uc2  (500570.BY) is down 3.3% at INR1,304.00 and ICICI Bank (532174.BY) is down 1.2% at INR1,117.00. The Sensex is likely to find support at 19,890 and face resistance at 20,220, according to Dow Jones technical analysis. (sudeep.jain@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0947 GMT [Dow Jones] Greece five year sovereign CDS is trading 16.5bps wider at 1010bps this morning after blowing out 30bps Thursday on the back of a report it may be forced to restructure its debts after 2013, Markit says. The Greece levels are dragging out the SovX index to near all time highs, at 208.5bps. Other sovereign CDS are slightly wider on the day. Portugal CDS is 3.8bps wider at 500bps, Spain CDS only marginally wider at 350bps, Italy CDS 2.3bps wider at 238.5bps and Belgium CDS 4.7bps wider at 222.5bps. Ireland CDS has pulled in 6.2bps to 600bps. (irene.chapple@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0942 GMT [Dow Jones] India overnight indexed swaps are sharply higher, driven by a persistent liquidity crunch in the banking system while higher-than-expected food inflation Thursday adds to the paying interest, says a foreign bank trader. The 1-year OIS rate is at 7.06%/7.09% vs 6.96%/6.99% last close while the 5-year OIS rate is at 7.72%/7.74% vs 7.64%/7.66% last close. "Swaps have been trading independently of bond yields on a hawkish rate view based on inflationary expectations. Despite lower yields today, swaps are higher and the market is still looking to play from the paid side irrespective of liquidity easing steps like bond buybacks by the RBI," the trader says. He expects the pace of uptrend in swaps to slow next week due to the absence of a weekly debt sale which will take pressure off banks liquidity. (khushita.vasant@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0936 GMT [Dow Jones] India government bonds are higher on bullish cut-offs at INR60 billion debt sale, a trader with a primary dealership says. Second-most traded 8.08% 2022 bond, which was part of the auction, rises to 100.28 after the cut-offs vs 100.20 before. However, the 7.17% 2015 bond, which was also auctioned, slips a tad on higher-than-expected cut-off yields. The RBI sets the cut-off yield for the 2015 bond at 7.87% vs 7.85% estimated in a Dow Jones poll, while it sets the cut-off for the 2022 bond at 8.04% vs 8.05% expected. The trader tips the 2022 bond yield to trade in a 8.03%-8.06% range vs 8.06% last close. (khushita.vasant@dowjones.com) [ 12-24-10 0748ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101224e6co0005e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
