\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Flat, As Risk Of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Nears\b0\par\par\uc2 1,314 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 2010\par 12:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1151 GMT [Dow Jones] Chile's peso was trading virtually unchanged at a 31-month high against the USD Wednesday morning, as market participants tread more cautiously, the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  approaching levels thought to merit an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Exporters have long clamored for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as they argue the peso's strong appreciation this year hurts their competitiveness abroad. Traders see an increased risk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the peso strengthens to CLP460-CLP465. In recent trading the peso was trading at CLP468.50 to the dollar, versus Tuesday's close of CLP468.70, according to data provided by local newswire Valor Futuro. (anthony.esposito@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1143 GMT 0000 GMT (Dow Jones) The decline in core Canadian CPI and the fact that 2 of the last 3 M&A deals over the last 7 days involving a Canadian Corporate (TD/Chrysler Finance and BMO/Wisconsin) have been CAD negative have stopped the Loonie in its tracks vs the USD and AUD notes Lloyds Bank Corporate Markets. However, the bank says sustained bounce in crude oil above $90/bbl may spark life back into CAD. USD/CAD now trades at 1.0123, AUD/CAD at 1.0120. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1132 GMT [Dow Jones] Euro Overnight Index Average fixed lower Tuesday at 0.391% versus Monday's 0.398%. Wednesday, the interbank overnight rate is trading narrower between 0.28% and 0.35% vs 0.25% and 0.35% Tuesday. A trader points to the favorable liquidity in the market keeping rates low. The ECB on Wednesday allotted EUR149.466 billion at a 98-day refinancing \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Earlier Wednesday, 3-month Euribor fixed at 1.021% vs 1.022% Tuesday. (matthias.goldschmidt@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1121 GMT [Dow Jones] The EUR149.5 billion allotted by the ECB at its last 3-month tender of 2010 is above consensus expectations of EUR100 billion and the news helps bring EUR/USD off the day's highs, notes RBC. RBC says EUR/USD just managed to close above its 200-day MA Tuesday but that level, 1.3096, is now looming large again. EUR/USD trades at 1.3145 within the day's 1.3080-1.3183 range. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1115 GMT [Dow Jones] Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  suggests rate hikes will be needed in the short term, given the "far less favorable" outlook for inflation. The Brazilian real gains to BRL1.692 at 1110 GMT, according to \uc2 Telekurs\uc2  via Factset, from Tuesday's close of BRL1.6975. The yield on Brazil's January 2012 interest rate futures contract rises to 12.07% from Tuesday's close of 11.99%. (matthew.cowley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1112 GMT [Dow Jones] India government bonds are down, but off session lows as traders cover short positions and dip into higher yields, but trading volumes remain thin, a state-run bank trader says. The most-traded 8.13% 2022 bond is at 100.70 from 100.59 intraday and 100.83 at the previous close. "Market sentiment was hurt after the RBI's comments that the upside risks to inflation are rising, but I think they took respite that the RBI is willing to take further steps to alleviate the discomfort caused by persistently tight liquidity among banks," the trader says. He tips the 2022 bond in a 100.60-100.80 band for the rest of the session. On Monday, banks borrowed a record INR1.59 trillion from the RBI's twin discount windows, which traders say was an all-time high. (khushita.vasant@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1100 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/INR touches an over one-week low of 45.07 on consistent exporter selling despite marginal losses in local stocks, a trader at a privately run bank says. The pair is at 45.10 from 45.23 late Tuesday. A trading head at a foreign bank adds a telecom company may have sold USD, pulling the pair lower even though the EUR/USD has come off its session highs. He notes trading volumes have thinned as the weekend approaches and foreign banks square positions before the year ends. He tips the pair in a 44.90-45.30 band for the rest of the week. The Sensex is down 0.2%. (khushita.vasant@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1053 GMT [Dow Jones] Citi says the EUR4-to-EUR5 billion of Portuguese debt that China will reportedly buy compares with a total of EUR17 billion of net supply that Citi's rate strategy team believes will be issued in 2011. The bank says net supply in the 1Q alone is projected at EUR6 billion, so the sums mentioned may help reduce funding pressures at the start of the year and so would be a small euro positive, if anything. EUR/USD now at 1.314. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1048 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/INR implied volatilities are trading slightly lower as the spot pair remains trapped in a tight range, with the holiday season dampening volumes in the pair, says a trader with a foreign bank. The one-month ATMF's are at 8.60%/9.20% from 8.60%/9.40% late Tuesday. "Volumes have been low, with some pressure obviously on gamma with many traders on vacation," says the trader, tipping volatilities to remain tepid over the next few sessions, with the one-week contract unlikely to trade beyond 8% from a bid-ask of 7.25%/8.75% currently. (bijou.george@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1047 GMT [Dow Jones] India's overnight indexed swaps are higher after a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said the upside risks to inflation are rising and the downside risk to growth is abating, which traders say gives RBI reason to lift interest rates, a foreign bank trader says. The one-year OIS rate is at 6.89%/6.93% from 6.84%/6.87% late Tuesday and the five-year OIS rate at 7.58%/7.62% from 7.50%/7.53%. "Factors like tight liquidity in banks, elevated inflation levels, robust growth and a gasoline price hike translate into paying interest. Swap rates stabilized a little when RBI announced bond buybacks of INR480 billion last week, but the bias is on the upside in the near-term," the trader says, adding investors are running thin positions ahead of year-end book closing. He tips the one-year OIS to peak at 7% and the five-year OIS to peak at 7.75% this week. (khushita.vasant@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1029 GMT [Dow Jones] The Monetary Policy Council of Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep its key interest rate unchanged at 3.50% at its Wednesday meeting, ING says. The MPC is probably still worried about excessive capital inflows and would be satisfied with headline CPI at 2.7%, being close to its 2.5% target. Other data, like flat core inflation having stayed at 1.2% for months as well as moderate wage growth, also support flat rates, ING says. (malgorzata.halaba@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1027 GMT [Dow Jones] Greece/10-year bund spread is flat on Wednesday at 905 bps with trading close to frozen. Combined turnover is a paltry EUR1M on the local HDAT and European trading platform. "The market is close to frozen due to seasonal factors given the upcoming holidays, with most participants having closed their positions and waiting for the new year to adopt a fresh strategy," says a senior local bond trader. "The threat by Fitch on Tuesday to cut Greece to junk, although not entirely unexpected, has added even more caution in investors' minds," he adds. (nick.skrekas@dowjones.com) [ 12-22-10 0651ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101222e6cm0006s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
