\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Strong copper puts off  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  peso  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 799 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2010\par 15:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 * Bank to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  only if strong peso lacks support\par \par \uc2 * Record copper prices bolster fundamentals of peso rally\par \par \uc2 By Brad Haynes\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Dec 17 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rein in a sharply appreciating peso as long as record prices of the country's top export, copper, continue underpinning the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rally.\par \par \uc2 This week surging copper prices have pushed the peso <CLP=CL> to new 30-month highs below 475 pesos per dollar for the first time since Oct. 13, renewing calls for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action from lawmakers and businessmen.\par \par \uc2 But bank president Jose De Gregorio reiterated to Congress on Tuesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be effective only if the peso were unmoored from long-term drivers, citing ineffective recent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by other central banks. For more see [ID:nN14274122].\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the best performer in Latin America this year, gaining 15 percent since June as the price of copper <HGH1> has climbed over 30 percent to hit new records above $4/lb on strong Chinese demand, boosting dollar revenues. The peso is tracking the weekly movement of copper prices closer than it has for two years, according to Thomson Reuters data.\par \par \uc2 "When the price of copper was at $3.50 (per pound), the level for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would probably have been 470 pesos (per dollar), because past that we would be getting away from fundamentals," said BBVA Chile economist Alejandro Puente.\par \par \uc2 "But with a much higher price of copper now, I see the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  probably \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a stronger exchange rate, for example 450 pesos (per dollar)." <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAKE-A-LOOK at Chile's economic recovery      [ID:nN30113748]\par For a graphic on the peso rally:   \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/mux99q"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/mux99q }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Central banks from Brazil to Thailand have carried out costly dollar purchases to stem their rallying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which have risen this year as investors pour money into higher-yielding emerging markets. Few of those attempts, however, have achieved lasting results.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 De Gregorio has said repeatedly that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  does not rule out entering the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if it were justified by a temporary misalignment of the peso, but the effect of the bank chief's verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is diminishing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The peso's strength has helped contain inflation in recent months by keeping down the effective cost of imports. This has allowed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to slow the pace of its interest rate hikes from 50 basis points to 25 basis points and to consider a brief pause in its monetary tightening cycle.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  raised its benchmark interest rate by 25 basis points to 3.25 percent on Thursday, its seventh consecutive rate increase, to keep up with an economy expected to grow over 5 percent this year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 COPPER ALIGNMENT\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's last direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  came in early 2008 when the peso strengthened past 430 per dollar, trading 9 percent stronger than today's nominal exchange rate at a time when copper was 5 percent weaker.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  came within weeks of the fall of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bear Stearns\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which precipitated a nearly 70 percent collapse in copper prices and compounded the depreciation of the peso, which lost more than a third of its value by the end of 2008.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The greatest risk of direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  today may be a sharp drop in copper prices without a corresponding depreciation of the peso, suggesting a disconnection from fundamentals.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  eventually \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , it is likely to announce a calendar of dollar purchases as it did in 2008 rather than set a target exchange rate.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But copper is not the only long-term fundamental supporting the peso's bullish trend. Chile's economy is now growing far more vigorously than two years ago while more developed economies are mired in a slow recovery, further underpinning peso strength.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile De Gregorio told lawmakers the current account is near neutral this year, meaning the peso's rally is not driven by speculative capital flows seen in other emerging economies.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Still, several analysts argue that a peso approaching 460 per dollar, whatever the cause, is the strongest level acceptable to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the short term.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But Chilean authorities have a limited arsenal to battle the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation. After cutting red tape and boosting hedging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for small exporters hurting from the stronger peso, Finance Minister Felipe Larrain acknowledged that taming the peso is a daunting task.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The exchange rate is a topic of concern for the government, but the dollar's weakness is a global problem," he said in an interview with state television on Friday. (Editing by Alonso Soto and Chizu Nomiyama)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CHILE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -PESO/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|C|MTL  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101220e6ch000vl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
